</node>
<node id="&quot;TENDERER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Tenderer is an individual or organization submitting a bid for a contract, responsible for ensuring all documentation requirements are met according to the checklist provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Tenderer refers to a company or individual interested in participating in the tender process and attending the pre-tender meeting."&lt;SEP&gt;"A tenderer refers to an entity or individual submitting a bid, which may be involved in inappropriate conducts and subject to regulating actions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenderers are individuals or organizations submitting bids for public works projects, required to deposit their tenders in the Tender Box before the specified closing time."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Tenderer is an individual or organization that may have questions about the precise meaning of items in the documents and can seek clarification from designated officers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cd345cf9a46f3f5c66ee8c178fe17aed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6502b9ed785b83b9a40ac91777278ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61c2f6f64e3310551b7f9deba4dfe97d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6f1c507a5f83ea7cc30c5ceefa06210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d53f0499b320835ae79f654161939981</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 49}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 77}]</data>
</node>
