  <data key="d2">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 23}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIRED AND HIRE-PURCHASE CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hired and hire-purchase plant involves leasing or purchasing machinery for use on the site, often with specific terms outlined in contracts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR OR HIS REPRESENTATIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Maintenance Surveyor or his representative is a role that issues certifications, specifically Certificates of Completion."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 39}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Constructional Plant includes appliances or things required for executing works but excludes materials forming part of permanent work or vehicles transporting personnel or Constructional Plant to/from the site."&lt;SEP&gt;"Constructional Plant includes equipment and materials intended to be supplied, used, or constructed as part of executing works according to the contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Constructional Plant includes machinery or equipment used in the execution of works, needing proper care during the Maintenance Period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Constructional Plant includes machinery, equipment, and other tools necessary for completing works under the contract, which becomes property of the Employer upon certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Constructional Plant refers to all appliances used in construction, which are part of the materials and equipment involved in completing Works Orders."&lt;SEP&gt;"Constructional Plant refers to equipment and materials brought onto the site by the Contractor for construction purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Constructional Plant refers to machinery and equipment used for construction activities that might be a factor in determining whether an extension of time is warranted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Constructional Plant refers to machinery and equipment used in construction projects that may be owned by the Contractor but can also involve third-party ownership requiring Maintenance Surveyor's consent."&lt;SEP&gt;"Constructional Plant refers to machinery or equipment used in the construction process that may be hired or purchased under specific conditions set by the Employer and Contractor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Constructional Plant refers to machinery, equipment, or tools required for construction works and may be subject to patent rights."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 59}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKS ORDER WITH AN ESTIMATED VALUE NOT EXCEEDING THE AMOUNT STATED IN THE APPENDIX TO THE FORM OF TENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This product is specifically referred to as a Complaint Chit if its value does not exceed the limit mentioned, indicating it's a smaller order within the larger scope of Works Orders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 35}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKS ORDER ISSUED UNDER THE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event here refers to the issuance of specific orders for work that are part of the overall contract and completion process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 40}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Maintenance Certificate is a document that might be issued as part of the process to ensure proper maintenance or completion of works, but its exact nature isn't fully described here."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Certificate is a final document stating that all required works have been completed and approved by the Maintenance Surveyor after the expiry of the Maintenance Period."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Certificate is an event where, upon issuance as provided in Clause 86, certain guarantees or deposited sums may become voidable according to Sureties or Security clause (12)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The maintenance certificate is a document issued by the Maintenance Surveyor stating that all work of repair, reconstruction, and rectification have been completed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba22dc0a0fc19429a484bb41c261d34</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 39}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FORFEITURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Forfeiture refers to a potential legal action where rights under the contract can be forfeited due to certain breaches by either party, indicating it's an important clause with significant consequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"The event of forfeiture occurs if certain conditions related to the Contractor's performance or financial status under the contract are met, leading to potential termination of the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9ba22dc0a0fc19429a484bb41c261d34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIAL RISKS 32 FRUSTRATION 33&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These terms refer to specific clauses in the contract dealing with unforeseen circumstances and disruptions that could affect the performance of work or obligations under the Contract, indicating potential legal and operational challenges."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SETTLEMENT OF DISPUTES 33&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to mechanisms for resolving disagreements between parties involved in the contract, which is a critical aspect of any contractual agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"This social science/industry event refers to mechanisms for resolving disagreements between parties involved in the contract, which is a critical aspect of any contractual agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SERVICE OF NOTICES 34&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The service of notices is an important procedural step within the contract, indicating formal communication and adherence to legal procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFAULT OF THE EMPLOYER 35&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event refers to scenarios where the Employer fails to meet its obligations under the Contract, which could lead to various consequences as outlined in this clause."&lt;SEP&gt;"This social science/industry event refers to scenarios where the Employer fails to meet its obligations under the Contract, which could lead to various consequences as outlined in this clause."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The General Conditions of Contract are a set of overarching rules and terms that govern all aspects of the contract between parties involved, providing a comprehensive framework for their interactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The General Conditions of Contract are part of the contractual agreement that outlines standard terms and conditions applicable to both parties involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"The General Conditions of Contract are the primary document governing the relationship between parties and outlining standard provisions for construction projects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION 1. (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This section provides definitions and interpretations which form the basis for understanding key terms in the Contract, essential for both legal interpretation and operational clarity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Certificate of Completion is a document issued by the Maintenance Surveyor or his representative to certify that all parts of a Works Order have been completed as per contract specifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Certificate of Completion is a document issued by the Maintenance Surveyor to indicate that the work has been substantially completed and passed final tests, marking the commencement of the Maintenance Period."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Certificate of Completion is a document under the Contract, which may not be required for certain steps in dispute resolution procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Certificate of Completion is an official document issued by the Maintenance Surveyor to confirm that all required work has been completed satisfactorily, marking the end of a Works Order cycle."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Certificate of Completion is a document issued under the contract indicating that all work has been completed, triggering obligations for removal or sale of constructional plant and surplus materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Certificate of Completion marks a significant event in the contract, indicating that all work has been completed to the Employer's satisfaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Certificate of Completion signifies the completion of work on the Site, triggering the Contractor's obligation to clear away surplus materials and rubbish."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c2d16f0534b8f7a9f0c286e3e24591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3e48c641bb7544fa8f59eeacc0c3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLAINT CHIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Complaint Chit is a Works Order with an estimated value not exceeding a specified amount, used for payment purposes similar to a regular Works Order."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Complaint Chit is a document used for claiming payment, endorsed by the Contractor and submitted with supporting documents when required."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Complaint Chit is a document used in the process of submitting dimension books for work completed, possibly related to complaints or disputes about the work done."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Complaint Chit, being an alternative term for certain small value Works Orders, indicates specific types of work orders and their simplified handling within the larger framework of the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 35}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLETION OF A WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The completion of all that part of the Works included in one Works Order signifies the successful conclusion of individual tasks under contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"This event refers to the completion of all parts included in one Works Order, indicating progress milestones within the contract scope."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 40}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLETION OF THE WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Completion of the Works is defined as the overall conclusion of all issued Works Orders under the Contract, marking its full execution and potential finalization."&lt;SEP&gt;"The completion of all Works Orders issued under the Contract represents the overall project's successful culmination, encompassing multiple parts and phases."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 40}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIRED AND HIRE-PURCHASE CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT 27&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This product refers to construction equipment that can be hired or purchased for use in executing works orders as per contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 60}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER'S EXPENSE IN ENTERING INTO HIRE OR HIRE-PURCHASE AGREEMENT 28&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These events refer to the financial obligations of the Employer when engaging with hiring or purchasing agreements for Constructional Plant, indicating specific cost and responsibility areas within the Contract."</data>
