</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS 29&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/PAYMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These events refer to interim payment processes within the Contract, indicating regular financial transactions between parties for ongoing work progress."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 40}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORRECTION AND WITHHOLDING OF CERTIFICATES 30&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This event involves correcting or withholding certification documents as part of the contract management process, ensuring accuracy in documentation and compliance with terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 39}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPROVAL WORKS 30&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Approval Works is a term indicating formal acceptance processes for completed work orders under the Contract, signifying completion milestones and quality assurance measures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICES 34&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT/DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Notices are formal communications within the Contract framework, indicating important procedural steps and legal requirements for maintaining transparency and accountability among all parties."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Contract refers to a formal agreement between the Contractor and the Employer detailing terms such as material supply, work execution, and financial obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contract is a document outlining terms and conditions for executing works, including rates, obligations, and instructions from the Maintenance Surveyor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contract is a formal agreement outlining responsibilities and obligations of both Contractor and Employer regarding works and payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contract is a legal agreement between parties defining their roles and responsibilities in executing works, including liability clauses for damage or loss."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contract is an agreement detailing the terms of work or services provided by the Contractor to the Employer, subject to review and decision-making processes involving the Maintenance Surveyor and potentially an arbitrator."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contract outlines the requirements, examinations, measurements, tests, and responsibilities of both the Contractor and Maintenance Surveyor regarding materials and workmanship on the Works."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contract refers to a comprehensive set of documents including Articles of Agreement, Tender, Drawings, General Conditions of Contract, Special Conditions if any, Specification and Schedule of Rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contract refers to the legal agreement between parties defining their obligations related to the Works, including maintenance responsibilities and conditions for suspension or continuation of works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 35}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACT AREA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Contract Area refers to a specific site where works are to be executed, which includes examining existing roads or other means of communication, ground conditions, and general information necessary for tendering."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contract Area specifies the geographical scope of work under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cost includes reasonable expenditures including overheads and depreciation but excludes profit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DRAWINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Drawings are detailed plans required for the execution of works, which may be requested by the contractor and must be available for inspection by relevant parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Drawings are part of the Contract Documents that need to be prepared and executed by the Contractor in accordance with specific clauses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Drawings are technical blueprints or specifications provided in the Contract, subject to modifications approved by the Maintenance Surveyor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Drawings refer to visual representations or blueprints used in specifying project requirements, which may be referenced but not necessarily included in the Schedule of Rates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b57445949baa2153e0f9f67f999456b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 13}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMERGENCY WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Emergency Work is an unforeseen task that requires immediate attention, for which the Contractor must have available workmen and plant at all times without extra charge except as detailed in the Contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency Work is any work classified as such by the Maintenance Surveyor and requires immediate attention."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency Work refers to urgent remedial or other work that needs to be carried out due to accidents, failures, or other unforeseen events affecting the Works."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency Work refers to urgent tasks ordered by the Maintenance Surveyor that require immediate commencement without delay unless otherwise instructed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency Work refers to urgent tasks ordered by the Maintenance Surveyor, which must be commenced immediately without delay."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1ba1c6b232e9a68005845d332fa7552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GENERAL HOLIDAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A General Holiday includes Sundays and other days declared as holidays by law under the Holidays Ordinance."&lt;SEP&gt;"A General Holiday is a day when normal work may be carried out but does not count towards time for completion without specific authorization."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 38}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maintenance Period is a specific time frame defined in the contract where any defects must be identified and addressed, typically lasting up to 14 days from its expiration date."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maintenance Period refers to a specific timeframe during which certain obligations and responsibilities are in effect under the contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maintenance Period refers to a specific timeframe during which obligations for maintenance and permanent reinstatement are in effect before full occupation takes place."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Period is a defined timeframe after work completion during which the Contractor remains responsible for any outstanding works or issues related to site care."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Period is a specific time frame during and after which certain rights and responsibilities are exercised, such as payment of sub-contractors directly by the Employer or assignment of obligations from nominated sub-contractors to the Employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Period is a specific timeframe during which defects or issues with the works can be identified and addressed before final certification."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Period is a specified duration calculated from the completion of Works Orders, certified by the Maintenance Surveyor according to Clause 56."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Period is a specified timeframe after completion of work during which any outstanding issues can be addressed as per contract terms and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Period is an event during which defects or imperfections may be identified and addressed, lasting up to 14 days after its expiration."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Period is an event during which the Contractor must complete any outstanding works as directed by the Maintenance Surveyor after receiving a Certificate of Completion."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Period is an event that starts from the date stated in a Certificate of Completion, marking when parts of the Works are considered complete and ready for permanent occupation or use."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c2d16f0534b8f7a9f0c286e3e24591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Nominated Sub-contractor is an entity contracted under the main contract, potentially causing delays if they fail to commence or carry out work in due time."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Nominated Sub-contractor is an entity selected by the Maintenance Surveyor for specific tasks, potentially with differing contractual terms from standard forms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nominated Sub-contractor is an organization contracted for services including construction, completion, maintenance and supply as per the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HONG KONG DOLLARS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hong Kong dollars refers to the currency used for payment as per the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAWS OF HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL SYSTEM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Contract is governed by and construed according to the laws currently in force in Hong Kong, indicating legal jurisdiction over the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE'S DELEGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Delegation of duties by the Maintenance Surveyor to his/her Representative is an event that requires written confirmation before it becomes effective."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 43}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 70}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTOR'S ASSIGNMENT OR SUB-LETTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The events of assigning or sub-letting works by the Contractor are regulated under specific conditions and require approval from the Employer and Maintenance Surveyor, respectively."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 43}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 70}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A sub-contractor is a party that may be employed by the Contractor to perform work on the site, subject to approval from the Maintenance Surveyor."&lt;SEP&gt;"A sub-contractor is an organization that works under the Contractor, providing services or materials related to the Works."&lt;SEP&gt;"A sub-contractor is an organization working under the Contractor and subject to Maintenance Surveyor's authority for access and work inspections."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE AND/OR WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Site and/or Works refer to the physical location or project area where construction activities are taking place."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIAL CONDITION OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Special Condition of Contract refers to specific terms within a contract that require certain actions from the Contractor regarding insurance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Special Conditions of Contract provide specific terms that may override General Conditions, indicating variability in contract agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specifications provide detailed instructions and requirements for executing works based on drawings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Specification outlines detailed descriptions of works or materials, guiding the Contractor's execution and measurement procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Specification provides detailed descriptions and technical data for materials, workmanship, etc., that are part of the contract documents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b57445949baa2153e0f9f67f999456b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62865738eafa658463c1c26212a98b20</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 80}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCHEDULE OF RATES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT, TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Schedule of Rates is a document containing pricing and specifications for work items that can be executed by Nominated Sub-contractors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Schedule of Rates is a document detailing measurement instructions and payment rates for work executed under the Contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Schedule of Rates is a document listing costs or pricing details related to project components not explicitly shown in Drawings but referenced by the Maintenance Surveyor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Schedule of Rates provides payment rates for work executed under the contract, subject to potential amendments as per the Contractor's tender."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Schedule of Rates provides pricing details for measuring and valuing work under each Works Order."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b57445949baa2153e0f9f67f999456b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62865738eafa658463c1c26212a98b20</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 80}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAUSE 64&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clause 64 is a mathematical clause used for valuing expenses related to work or materials, likely involving calculations or certifications for payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clause 64 is referenced for valuing investigations conducted by the Contractor when defects are not his liability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clause 64 likely deals with valuation and certification procedures for expenses incurred due to ambiguities or discrepancies, ensuring fair compensation as per contract terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clause 64 likely refers to a mathematical calculation or valuation process used in determining expenses related to examinations, measurements, or tests not provided for in the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62865738eafa658463c1c26212a98b20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 13}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPERINTENDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Superintendence refers to the oversight and management of construction activities by the Contractor, which is a critical responsibility under the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMBIGUITIES OR DISCREPANCIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT/SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ambiguities or discrepancies refer to unclear or conflicting terms in contract documents that may require clarification from the Maintenance Surveyor for proper interpretation and execution of the project."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION OF CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The provision of constructional plant involves supplying necessary equipment, materials, etc., required for the works as per contractual obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKMEN OR AGENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workmen or agents refer to personnel employed by sub-contractors who are subject to the Contractor's responsibility and accountability under the Contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR INSTRUCTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT/CONTRACT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Instructions from the Maintenance Surveyor clarify ambiguities, resolve discrepancies, and guide contractors on project execution and compliance with contract conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;14 DAYS PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TIME/SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A 14-day period is specified for various actions such as receipt of requests, responses to instructions, or prohibitions against sub-letting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMBIGUITY OR DISCREPANCY RESOLUTION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS/SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The ambiguity or discrepancy resolution process involves the Maintenance Surveyor issuing instructions to clarify unclear terms in contract documents ensuring clear and consistent interpretation by all parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION OF SUPERINTENDENCE (CLAUSE 18)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTRACT CLAUSE/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Provision of superintendence as per Clause 18 refers to the Contractor's responsibility for overseeing work, including sub-contractors' activities and ensuring compliance with contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR POWER TO INSTRUCT REMOVAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"POWER/SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Maintenance Surveyor has the authority to instruct the removal of any sub-contractor from the Site or Works if deemed necessary for project management, indicating a significant supervisory role in construction projects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTOR'S LIABILITY AND RESPONSIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Contractor remains liable for acts, defaults, and neglects of their sub-contractors as fully as if they were the Contractor’s own actions, highlighting strict accountability measures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FURNISHING FULL PARTICULARS TO MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCEDURE/SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contractors are required to furnish detailed information about any sub-contractor employed or planned for employment on Works upon request by the Maintenance Surveyor, ensuring transparency and compliance with contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIAL CONDITION OF CONTRACT (CLAUSE 64)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTRACT CLAUSE/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Special Conditions of Contract may provide specific provisions that override General Conditions, indicating flexibility in contractual agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S VALUATION AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE/SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Maintenance Surveyor has the power to value and certify expenses incurred by Contractors due to ambiguities or discrepancies, ensuring fair compensation as per contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNREASONABLE EXERCISE OF POWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LEGAL/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Powers exercised by the Maintenance Surveyor must not be unreasonable, indicating a balance between authority and fairness in project management."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION OF CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT (SUB-CLAUSE 2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTRACT CLAUSE/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-clause 2 specifies conditions under which sub-contractors can provide constructional plant without explicit prohibition by the Maintenance Surveyor, highlighting flexibility and cooperation in project execution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S INSTRUCTIONS FOR AMBIGUITIES OR DISCREPANCIES (SUB-CLAUSE 5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCEDURE/SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Instructions from the Maintenance Surveyor clarify ambiguous terms and resolve discrepancies between contract documents, ensuring clear interpretation by all parties involved."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION OF SUPERINTENDENCE (CLAUSE 18) - CONTRACTOR'S RESPONSIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTRACT CLAUSE/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The provision of superintendence as per Clause 18 emphasizes the Contractor’s ongoing responsibility for overseeing work and sub-contractors, ensuring compliance with contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-LETTING PROHIBITION (CLAUSE 2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTRACT CLAUSE/INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-clause 2 prohibits sub-letting without explicit written approval from the Maintenance Surveyor within a specified period, highlighting strict control measures over project execution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S ROLE IN CONTRACT INTERPRETATION AND RESOLUTION OF AMBIGUITIES (SUB-CLAUSE 5)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE/SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Maintenance Surveyor plays a crucial role in interpreting ambiguous terms and resolving discrepancies between contract documents, ensuring clear communication and consistent application of contractual provisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Tender is a formal bid or proposal submitted by the Contractor to undertake specific work orders under certain conditions and terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Tender refers to an event where contractors submit bids or proposals for undertaking specific works as per contract terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Tender refers to an official bid or proposal submitted by the Contractor in response to a request for work under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 35}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DRAWINGS PROVIDED BY THE CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are technical drawings and documents submitted by the Contractor for work execution, subject to approval from the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 13}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Works refer to specific projects or tasks that need to be executed under the contract. They can also denote a location where these works will take place."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Works refer to the construction or project that is being undertaken according to a specific contract and can be partially or fully completed by either the Contractor or the Employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Works refer to the construction or repair projects being undertaken, which include various parts that may need inspection or modification."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Works refer to the construction or work being performed according to specific instructions and orders outlined in the Contract and Works Order."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Works refer to the construction project where daywork is being carried out, involving various activities such as labor, material usage, and progress monitoring."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term 'Works' refers to the main project or construction activities being carried out by the Contractor and may include sub-contracted tasks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works refer to a set of construction or engineering tasks carried out by the Contractor under specific contractual obligations, which can be partially completed and certified for use before full completion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works refer to specific constructional tasks and projects carried out on-site, requiring careful management of safety and order."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works refer to the construction or installation tasks that are being carried out under a contractual agreement and require maintenance during and after completion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works refer to the construction or services that are contracted between the Employer and Contractor, which may be subject to review and decision-making processes involving the Maintenance Surveyor and potentially an arbitrator."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works refer to the construction projects being executed as per the contract, potentially involving various types of work and temporary structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works refer to the construction projects that need to be completed as per the Contract terms, including excavation, site preparation, and execution of specific tasks outlined in the contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works refers to a construction or maintenance project site where various tasks are performed by contractors and other parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works refers to a specific site where construction or maintenance activities are taking place."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works refers to specific construction or maintenance projects that are subject to various regulatory and procedural requirements as outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 68}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INFORMATION NOT TO BE DIVULGED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES/TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to confidential information provided by either party during the course of the contract, which must remain within the bounds of the agreement and cannot be used or disclosed outside its intended purpose without consent."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 13}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HONG KONG GOVERNMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hong Kong Government acts as a depositary for security sums provided by the Contractor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hong Kong Government refers to a governmental body that has an accounting service department where security deposits can be made or released."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 33}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARTICLES OF AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Articles of Agreement are documents to be prepared and executed by the Contractor at their expense, in forms provided by the Employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 39}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIRECTOR OF ACCOUNTING SERVICES, HONG KONG GOVERNMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Director is responsible for managing the deposit and release process related to the Contract as per the terms agreed upon with the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 33}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S INSTRUCTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Instructions provided by the Maintenance Surveyor are detailed guidelines that must be followed during the execution of works, covering both mentioned and implied matters within the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary Works are specific items or structures created during the execution phase that may be subject to damage claims but not under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Works are specific types of construction or installation that may be included in the scope of works under the contract, but their design and specification requirements must be clearly stated in the Contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Works are structures or facilities set up temporarily during construction activities that may include scaffolding, temporary roads, etc., necessary for proper execution of the project."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 68}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKS AND RATES AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The agreement covers all risks, liabilities, and obligations related to executing works as per the contract terms, ensuring compliance with Maintenance Surveyor's instructions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTHORIZED ENGLISH-SPEAKING AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An authorized English-speaking agent, approved by the Maintenance Surveyor, responsible for superintendence of the Works and receiving directions from the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-contractors are organizations or individuals working under the Contractor to execute parts of the works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 46}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 73}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TECHNICAL PERSONNEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Technical personnel refers to skilled and experienced workers in specific trades, employed by the Contractor for proper supervision of work execution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SKILLED LABOUR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Skilled labour includes specialized workers necessary for executing the Works properly and timely."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEMI-SKILLED LABOUR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Semi-skilled labour refers to workers with some training but not as highly skilled, also employed by the Contractor for work execution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNSKILLED LABOUR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Unskilled labour includes general laborers needed for executing the Works without specialized skills."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIALIST CONTRACTORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specialist Contractors are entities responsible for specific works on a site, ensuring safety and maintaining order."&lt;SEP&gt;"Specialist Contractors are subcontractors with specific expertise that operate independently within the site but do not fall under the direct responsibility of the main Contractor for safety and stability issues."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UTILITY UNDERTAKERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Utility Undertakers are involved in the maintenance of utilities on-site, contributing to overall safety measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Utility Undertakers are organizations responsible for providing essential services such as water, electricity, or gas to the site, operating separately from the main Contractor in terms of safety responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Site is another term for the location where the Works and related activities occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Site is a location where construction or maintenance activities are carried out by the Contractor as per the Works Orders."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Site is a physical location where construction or maintenance activities are taking place, subject to various regulations regarding labor records, fossil preservation, and facility provision for other contractors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Site is a physical location where works are performed, from which constructional plant, temporary buildings, and surplus materials must be removed after completion."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Site is a specific area where construction or maintenance activities take place and includes both completed works and ongoing operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Site is a specific location where construction or maintenance activities take place and materials are stored or used."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Site is a specific location where construction or maintenance activities take place under the contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Site is a specific location where work is being carried out under the contract agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Site is the location where work of permanent reinstatement and other activities take place, as mentioned throughout the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Site is the location where works are being carried out under the contract, subject to potential entry by the Employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Site is the physical location where works are being carried out and requires specific safety measures such as lighting, guards, fences, and warning signs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Site refers to a specific location where maintenance surveys are conducted and works are carried out by the Contractor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Site refers to the physical location where works are being carried out under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3e48c641bb7544fa8f59eeacc0c3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 30}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BENCH-MARKS, SITE-RAILS, PEGS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are tools used in setting-out to ensure the correct positioning of elements during construction or maintenance work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WATCHMEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Watchmen are personnel hired by the Contractor for security purposes at the Site, ensuring that safety and order are maintained as per Maintenance Surveyor's instructions or statutory requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR’S INSTRUCTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Instructions from the Maintenance Surveyor guide contractors on how to perform their duties correctly, including setting-out corrections and site management practices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTOR’S RESPONSIBILITY FOR STABILITY AND SAFETY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This concept outlines that the Contractor is fully responsible for ensuring the stability and safety of all operations on-site except those performed by Specialist Contractors or utility undertakers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ORDERLY STATE OF SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maintaining an orderly state at the site involves keeping it clean, organized, and safe to avoid hazards for everyone present."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIGHTS, GUARDS, FENCES, WARNING SIGNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are safety equipment provided by the Contractor to protect workers and visitors on-site from potential dangers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VARIATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Variation is an alteration in the scope of work that may require additional payment as detailed in the Contract, often arising due to errors or changes during construction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORRECTNESS OF POSITION, LEVEL, DIMENSIONS AND ALIGNMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This concept emphasizes the Contractor's responsibility for ensuring all parts of the Works are correctly positioned, leveled, dimensioned, and aligned according to reference points provided by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHECKING SETTING-OUT OR LINES/LEVELS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Checking process involves verifying setting-out accuracy through inspections conducted by the Maintenance Surveyor, which does not relieve the Contractor of their responsibility for correctness."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION OF INSTRUMENTS AND APPLIANCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Instruments and appliances are tools provided or maintained by the Contractor to ensure accurate setting-out during construction work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORRECTIVE ACTIONS DUE TO ERRORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"If errors in positioning, leveling, dimensions, or alignment appear during works progress, the Contractor must rectify them at their own expense unless based on incorrect data provided by the Maintenance Surveyor, which would be treated as a Variation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTOR’S DUTY TO RECTIFY ERRORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Contractor is obligated to correct any errors in setting-out or alignment without additional charge except for variations detailed in the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION OF EMERGENCY STAFF WITHOUT EXTRA CHARGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Emergency staff are provided by the Contractor at no extra cost, ensuring readiness for unforeseen tasks that may arise on-site."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORRECTNESS OF POSITION AND ALIGNMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ensuring correctness in positioning and alignment is a fundamental responsibility of the Contractor throughout the project to maintain quality standards as per Maintenance Surveyor's instructions or drawings provided by them."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION OF INSTRUMENTS FOR SETTING-OUT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Instruments used for setting-out are essential tools that must be provided and maintained by the Contractor to ensure accurate work execution."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 23}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE SAFETY MEASURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Safety measures include providing lights, guards, fences, warning signs, and maintaining an orderly state of the site to protect all persons on-site from potential hazards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATUTORY OR OTHER AUTHORITY REQUIREMENTS FOR PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Contractor must comply with any safety requirements set by competent statutory or other authorities to ensure proper protection of the Works during construction activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION AND MAINTENANCE OF SAFETY EQUIPMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Safety equipment such as lights, guards, fences, warning signs are provided and maintained by the Contractor for site security purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTOR’S ONGOING RESPONSIBILITY FOR SITE STABILITY AND SAFETY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Contractor must continuously ensure that all operations on-site are stable and safe, adhering to Maintenance Surveyor's instructions or statutory requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION OF WATCHMEN WHEN NECESSARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Watchmen hired by the Contractor provide security at the site when necessary as per Maintenance Surveyor’s or statutory authority’s instructions for protection purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE MANAGEMENT PRACTICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Site management practices involve maintaining order, providing safety equipment, and ensuring that all operations are conducted in a manner consistent with project requirements and regulatory standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROVISION OF WORKMEN AND PLANT FOR EMERGENCY WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workmen and plant provided by the Contractor must be available at no extra charge to execute emergency work as required, ensuring readiness for unforeseen tasks on-site."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORRECTNESS OF SETTING-OUT BASED ON PROVIDED DATA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The correctness of setting-out is based on data supplied by the Maintenance Surveyor; any errors arising from incorrect provided data are treated differently than those due to contractor negligence or misinterpretation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPECIALIST WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Specialist Works are specific tasks undertaken by Specialist Contractors that require particular attention to safety and maintenance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (4) OF THIS CLAUSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-Clause (4</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7a4656c68f6e92038fab565bd5849a14</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OUTBREAK OF WAR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An outbreak of war in which Hong Kong will be actively engaged."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 55}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INVASION OF HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The invasion of Hong Kong by an external force."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 55}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACT OF FOREIGN TERRORISTS IN HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Acts committed by foreign terrorists within the territory of Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 55}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIVIL WAR, REBELLION, REVOLUTION OR MILITARY OR USURPED POWER IN HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Events such as civil war, rebellion, revolution, or military takeover occurring within Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 55}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RIOT, COMMOTION OR DISORDER IN HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Acts of rioting, commotions, or disorder that do not involve the employees of specific contractors working on the project."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 55}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OCCUPATION BY EMPLOYER'S AGENTS, EMPLOYEES, TENANTS OR OTHER CONTRACTORS NOT EMPLOYED BY CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The occupation of parts of the works for purposes other than carrying out specialist works by employers' agents, employees, tenants, or non-contractor contractors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 55}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DAMAGE DUE TO MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S DESIGN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Damage directly resulting from the design work done by the maintenance surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEGLECT OR DEFAULT BY EMPLOYER OR THEIR EMPLOYEES AND AGENTS IN COURSE OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Acts of neglect or default committed by the employer, their employees, and agents during their employment period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDEMNIFICATION AGAINST LOSSES AND CLAIMS FOR INJURY OR DAMAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Contractor's obligation to indemnify the Employer against all losses, claims, damages, costs, charges, and expenses arising from injury or damage to persons or property during work execution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAKING GOOD OF PROPERTY DAMAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Contractor's responsibility to repair or compensate for any property damage caused by their actions or those of their employees/subcontractors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 55}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RECOMPENSE FOR EMPLOYEE INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compensation provided by the Contractor for injuries sustained by Employer’s employees due to work execution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPORTIONATE LIABILITY REDUCTION DUE TO CONTRIBUTORY ACTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The reduction in liability of the Contractor when the act or neglect of the Maintenance Surveyor, Employer, their respective agents, or employees contributes to damage, loss, or injury."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMANENT WORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Permanent Work refers to long-lasting construction elements, which design responsibility is excluded from the Contractor as per clause 25 of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC ROADS OR FOOTPATHS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public roads or footpaths are locations that may be affected by the execution of Works but do not fall under specific claims as per clause 26 of the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 65}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Properties refer to real estate, which can include both public and private lands potentially impacted during work execution without liability for certain damages or inconveniences."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 65}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC OR PRIVATE ROADS OR FOOTPATHS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are locations where access is regulated during construction activities, ensuring public convenience and safety."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSIONER FOR LABOUR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Commissioner for Labour is a role that may require notifications and forward copies to the Maintenance Surveyor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Commissioner for Labour is an individual responsible for receiving notifications of workman injuries as per the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, MACHINE, WORK METHOD OR MATERIAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These are items required for the Works and may be subject to patent rights and royalties as per contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PATENT RIGHTS, DESIGN, TRADEMARK OR NAME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to intellectual property protections that the Contractor must indemnify against infringement claims by the Employer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 64}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PATENT RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Patent Rights refer to legal protections for inventions, including articles, processes, or new technologies that may be incorporated into construction works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DESIGNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Designs are part of the protected rights and can include any creative work related to the Constructional Plant or machine."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRADEMARK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Trademark is a form of protection for brand names, logos, or other identifiers that may be used in construction works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NAME RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Name Rights refer to the legal protections related to specific names associated with protected inventions or technologies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MACHINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Machines are part of the Constructional Plant that can include any mechanical devices used in construction projects and may have associated patents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 59}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK METHOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Work Method is a specific technique or process for completing tasks, which might be protected by patent rights if it involves new technology or processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATERIAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Materials are any substances used in construction works and may have associated patents protecting their use or application methods."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TONNAGE ROYALTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tonnage Royalties refer to payments based on the weight of materials, which can be a financial aspect related to the procurement of resources for the project."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 26}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 63}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ROYALTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Royalties are payments made by the Contractor to owners of intellectual property rights in relation to the use or sale of their inventions or technologies used in construction works."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 24}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rent can refer to periodic payments for the use of resources, which may be part of agreements related to materials and equipment procurement."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 27}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Payments are financial transactions required by the Contractor as per contractual obligations or local regulations during construction works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 27}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TENDER SUBMISSION DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Tender Submission Date is a specific point in time when bids for contracts must be submitted, which can affect fee calculations and other financial aspects of the project."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEW FEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A New Fee refers to any additional charges imposed after the submission date that are at the expense of the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCREASE IN EXISTING FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Increase in Existing Fees is a situation where pre-existing fees related to construction materials or services have been raised, impacting the financial obligations of the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Contractor is a party required to comply with various enactments, regulations, and rules as specified in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contractor is responsible for maintaining site records, delivering labor returns to the Maintenance Surveyor's Representative, ensuring workmen do not damage or remove fossils, providing facilities to other contractors' workers, and clearing away surplus materials upon completion."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3e48c641bb7544fa8f59eeacc0c3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 41}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE DIARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Site Diary is a document maintained by the Maintenance Surveyor's Representative that records daily activities on-site including labor, plant usage, material use, utility consumption, work performed, and contractor instructions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 41}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOR RETURNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Labor Returns are detailed reports submitted to the Maintenance Surveyor showing the number of workers in different classes both for a specific day and over the preceding 24 hours."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 41}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENACTMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Enactments refer to laws or legislative provisions that must be adhered to by The Contractor during the Works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regulations are formal rules issued and enforced by a government authority, which The Contractor is required to follow for the duration of the Works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 43}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 69}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BY-LAWS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"By-laws refer to local or municipal regulations that must be followed during the course of the Works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUBLIC BODIES AND COMPANIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Public Bodies and Companies are entities whose rules and regulations The Contractor is required to comply with, as mentioned in Clause 31."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 43}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 69}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOCAL AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Local Authority refers to any local governing body that has the power to issue by-laws applicable during the Works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHINESE CHARACTERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chinese Characters are required for notices written in compliance with Government or other competent authority rules, indicating a need for bilingual communication on-site."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENGLISH LANGUAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LANGUAGE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"English is used alongside Chinese characters to ensure clear and comprehensive communication regarding site activities and regulatory requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S OFFICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maintenance Surveyor's Office is the designated location where records, including Site Diaries and Labor Returns, are submitted by The Contractor as per the instructions of the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE RECORD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Site Record refers to comprehensive documentation maintained by the Maintenance Surveyor that includes site diaries and other relevant information for project oversight and compliance verification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AUTHORIZED AGENT OR REPRESENTATIVE OF THE CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Authorized Agent or Representative of The Contractor signs site diaries to indicate agreement with recorded information or notes disagreements in writing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S DIRECTIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maintenance Surveyor’s Directive refers to the instructions and requirements issued by the Maintenance Surveyor for proper record-keeping, compliance verification, and project oversight during the Works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLIANCE VERIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compliance Verification is a process where The Contractor ensures adherence to all applicable enactments, regulations, by-laws, and rules as directed by the Maintenance Surveyor’s Representative."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDEMNIFICATION AGAINST PENALTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Indemnification against penalties refers to financial or legal protection provided by The Contractor to the Employer for any breaches of enacted laws, regulations, by-laws, and rules during the Works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PENALTIES AND LIABILITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Penalties and Liabilities are potential consequences that may arise from non-compliance with enactments, regulations, by-laws, or other applicable rules during the course of the Works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 41}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK CARRIED OUT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Work Carried Out refers to activities performed on-site as part of the maintenance or construction project that are subject to detailed documentation and compliance verification processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 23}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INSTRUCTIONS ISSUED TO THE CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Instructions Issued To The Contractor refer to directives provided by the Maintenance Surveyor's Representative for daily operations, record-keeping, and other site-related activities during the Works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LABOR ON-SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Labor on-site refers to workers engaged in various tasks related to maintenance or construction projects as documented in Site Diaries and Labor Returns."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 23}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLANT USAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Plant Usage includes the utilization of machinery, equipment, and other tools necessary for site operations that are recorded daily in Site Diaries."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 23}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATERIALS USED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Materials Used refers to construction materials or supplies utilized on-site as part of ongoing maintenance or construction activities documented in Site Diaries."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 0}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 26}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 63}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UTILITIES CONSUMPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Utilities Consumption includes the use of water, electricity, and other utilities necessary for site operations that are recorded daily in Site Diaries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 41}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORK PROGRESS AND QUALITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Work Progress and Quality refer to the overall advancement and standard of work on-site as documented by the Maintenance Surveyor's Representative through Site Diary entries and other records."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISAGREEMENTS IN WRITING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Disagreements in writing are instances where The Contractor’s Authorized Agent or Representative notes discrepancies with recorded information directly within Site Diaries to ensure transparency and accuracy of documentation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDUSTRIES INVOLVED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The industries involved include construction, maintenance, and possibly public works, as these activities are subject to detailed regulatory compliance and record-keeping requirements outlined in the text."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 44}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATORY COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regulatory Compliance refers to adherence by The Contractor to all relevant laws, regulations, by-laws, and rules during the course of the Works for proper project execution and oversight."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employer owns all fossils, coins, and other valuable items found on-site and requires the Contractor to report such discoveries and comply with Maintenance Surveyor's instructions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3e48c641bb7544fa8f59eeacc0c3c2e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 41}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOSSILS, COINS, ARTICLES OF VALUE OR ANTIQUITY, STRUCTURES, AND GEOLOGICAL OR ARCHAEOLOGICAL REMAINS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These items discovered on the Site belong to the Employer and must be reported and preserved according to Maintenance Surveyor's instructions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a3e48c641bb7544fa8f59eeacc0c3c2e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 30}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OFFERING GRATUITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is an event where the Contractor and its agents are prohibited from offering any form of advantage or bribe, with potential consequences for breach of this rule."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE CLEANLINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The concept involves maintaining a clean site as per Maintenance Surveyor's requirements, including providing sanitary facilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 30}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hong Kong is a location where certain events (such as invasion, civil war&lt;SEP&gt;"Hong Kong is a location where the labor conditions are specified and where passes for workpeople might be issued."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hong Kong is mentioned as a place where the registered office of companies might be located, and also possibly the site location for service of notices."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d995518579c80996691b5d1b66c19ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 64}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEPARTMENT OF LABOUR AND HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Department of Labour in Hong Kong is mentioned as the office where claims regarding wage payments can be filed and processed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 42}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMISSIONER FOR LABOUR, HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON/ROLE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Commissioner for Labour in Hong Kong is a role responsible for overseeing labor conditions and resolving disputes related to wages and employment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKPEOPLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES/PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Workpeople are the individuals employed by the Contractor who require passes to access the site or portions thereof, indicating their status as laborers in the worksite context."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TESTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Tests are a method used to examine, measure, or evaluate the quality of materials and workmanship as required by the Contract or ordered by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 13}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-clause (2) is an event where the Contractor must provide assistance for examining, measuring, or testing any work and samples of materials before incorporation into the Works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (A)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-clause (a) is an event where any expense relating to examinations, measurements, or tests ordered by the Maintenance Surveyor that show materials or workmanship are not in accordance with the Contract will be borne by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 43}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 69}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (B)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-clause (b) is an event where if a series of tests on any part of the Works indicate that the Contractor has failed to comply with the requirements, then the expense of complying with this Clause will be borne by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (C)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-clause (c) is an event where if any test or series of tests show that the Contractor has failed to comply with the Contract's requirements, then further or other tests as approved by the Maintenance Surveyor will be carried out at the Contractor's expense."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Access refers to the right granted to the Maintenance Surveyor and his authorized persons to enter various locations including the Works, Site, workshops, and places where materials or manufactured articles are stored or prepared by the Contractor or sub-contractors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE [GCCBWT] 45&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-clause [gccbwt] 45 is an event that grants access rights to the Maintenance Surveyor and his authorized persons at all times on the Works, Site, workshops, and places where materials or manufactured articles are stored or prepared by the Contractor or sub-contractors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 43}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 69}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAUSE 46 (1)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clause 46(1) describes an event where work cannot be covered up without prior approval from the Maintenance Surveyor or their Representative, requiring full opportunity for examination before covering up."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAUSE 47 (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clause 47(2) details another event involving uncovering and making openings in Works as directed by the Maintenance Surveyor, with responsibilities to reinstate parts of the Works accordingly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The term 'Maintenance Surveyor’s Order' is used in context of instructions or authorizations given by the Maintenance Surveyor for work execution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 30}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKS COMPLETION TIME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Works Completion Time refers to the duration within which works are expected to be completed, subject to possible extensions as per Clause 53."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 64}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NORMAL WORKING HOURS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Normal Working Hours are standard working times, outside which work requires permission from the Maintenance Surveyor unless it prevents injury or damage."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINUOUS WORKING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Continuous Working refers to the requirement by the Maintenance Surveyor to perform tasks 24 hours per day, as specified in Clause 52."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTENSION OF TIME FOR COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Extension of Time for Completion is a provision allowing delays due to unforeseen circumstances or orders from the Maintenance Surveyor, subject to notice and documentation requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCLEMENT WEATHER CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Inclement weather conditions are considered as an event that can cause delays in the progress of works, affecting the ability to proceed with construction activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STORM SIGNAL NO. 8 OR ABOVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hoisting a storm signal no. 8 or above is a specific condition indicating severe weather that could lead to work suspension and subsequent delay."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAUSE 5, CLAUSE 63, CLAUSE 57 (2) (A) TO (D), CLAUSE 63&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These clauses refer to specific conditions or events under which delays can be justified for an extension of time. They include instructions from the Maintenance Surveyor and variations in work orders."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UTILITY UNDERTAKING, DULY CONSTITUTED AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Utility undertakings or other duly constituted authorities are organizations that may impact construction by failing to commence or complete necessary works on schedule, potentially causing delays if not addressed proactively by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE, PORTION OF SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The site and its portions refer to specific areas where work is being carried out. Delays can occur due to issues related to access or conditions at these locations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAUSE 57 (2)(A) TO (D)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These clauses describe specific circumstances under which the contractor may not be entitled to an extension, such as suspension caused by certain events or conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR (CLAUSE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The organization known as the Maintenance Surveyor is responsible for overseeing work progress, granting extensions of time, and instructing on necessary steps to expedite work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-671cf14fabde451a853f4cb49e6a812f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GENERAL HOLIDAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"General Holidays are days when work is not expected to proceed as per standard contract terms, impacting the completion timeline."&lt;SEP&gt;"General holidays are days off that may affect the deadlines for submitting statements or lists, as specified within the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE OFFICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Site Offices are locations where contractors provide services such as offices and latrines until all outstanding works are completed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a0c2d16f0534b8f7a9f0c286e3e24591</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 66}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLETION CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Completion Certificate is a document issued by the Maintenance Surveyor certifying that certain parts of the works have been completed to satisfaction and can be used permanently."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUSPENSION ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Suspension Orders are directives from the Maintenance Surveyor instructing the Contractor to halt work for specific reasons, such as weather conditions or contractor defaults."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLAUSE 59(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SOCIAL SCIENCES"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clause 59(2) is a reference within the contract that defines certain exclusions from the term 'Works', indicating specific tasks not covered under this clause."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GROUND REINSTATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ground reinstatement refers to the process of restoring any disturbed ground after construction, which may or may not be included in a Certificate of Completion depending on its explicit mention."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUSPENSION LASTING MORE THAN 90 DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This is an event where work suspension exceeds 90 days, potentially triggering specific conditions and considerations within the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 21}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUSPENSION OF WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Suspension of Works refers to a situation where the progress of the Works is halted for more than 90 days on the order of the Maintenance Surveyor without permission to resume work within 90 days, potentially allowing the Contractor to serve notice and proceed with the works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY REINSTATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary reinstatement is a process involving the making good of any defects or imperfections in the temporary restoration of highways, roads, or ways until permanent reinstatement can be carried out by an appropriate authority or another party."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 28}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 64}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMANENT REINSTATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Permanent reinstatement refers to the final and complete repair work that may be undertaken by a relevant authority after the Maintenance Period has ended or when full occupation of the site is taken for permanent works."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 67}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFECT, IMPERFECTION OR FAULT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"These terms refer to issues that may arise in the work of permanent reinstatement which need investigation and rectification as per contractual obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b</data>
