  <data key="d1">"A Sub-contract is a specific type of agreement between parties, often involving different terms from standard forms and potentially leading to additional expenditure for the Contractor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sub-contracts are agreements entered into by the Contractor to execute specific portions of the works, incorporating certain clauses related to plant management and cost recovery."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
