</node>
<node id="&quot;OPENINGS TENDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The event of opening tenders involves actions taken by the Tender Opening Team as per procedures outlined in NTT A2 Procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2"></data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 45}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 72}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">The entity "Employer" refers to an organization or party that engages a contractor for specific works and holds significant responsibilities and rights throughout the contract period. The Employer is distinct from other parties such as the Maintenance Surveyor, but plays crucial roles in payment, work completion, indemnification, and dispute resolution.

Key aspects of the Employer's role include:
- Engaging contractors to undertake specified works.
- Acquiring property or materials upon delivery to the site and potentially receiving payments for surplus removal or sale.
- Having the authority to deduct overpayments from certificates issued by the Contractor due to various causes.
- Issuing Demand Notes for repayment if necessary.
- Ordering work or materials from specialists, including instructing the Contractor to enter into sub-contracts with nominated subcontractors using specific forms provided by them.
- Being a party that may receive claims related to delays in completion of works orders and having rights regarding payment and work completion.
- Contracting directly with companies or individuals not being utility undertakings for materials, plant, or equipment delivery.
- Indemnifying the Contractor against certain liabilities and paying for damages caused by special risks.
- Ensuring timely payments from the Main Contractor to maintain Subcontractor's ability to receive payments under subcontract agreements.
- Entering upon the site and expelling the contractor without avoiding the contract or releasing obligations, if necessary.
- Paying nominated sub-contractors directly and assigning obligations after the maintenance period ends.
- Being liable for claims considered valid by the Maintenance Surveyor.
- Providing information and executing works as per agreement terms.
- Receiving certification from the Maintenance Surveyor to make payments based on work completed.
- Potentially facing claims related to the use of their property, especially if they provide land or other resources for execution.

The Employer also has financial responsibilities such as making payments on behalf of the Contractor in scenarios where wage claims are not settled by the contractor. They have rights and powers under a contract including entering upon the site, expelling contractors without avoiding the contract, and retaining certain obligations even after termination. The Employer is involved in hiring or purchasing equipment for use on-site, managing costs related to such agreements, and ensuring completion of works despite potential contract terminations.

In summary, the Employer plays a multifaceted role as both an engaging party and a paying entity with significant oversight responsibilities over work execution, payment management, and dispute resolution.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02dce26d755dbc2a1f010f8cd0550db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-754aa01b6700b16ce9dfa955549688dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f34cc8c71a86a28ce1e2196a0e32a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba22dc0a0fc19429a484bb41c261d34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa9c6366e076e445101d83858797035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62cee928581076993e6dc7290419d468&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671cf14fabde451a8