<node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">A Maintenance Surveyor is an essential role within the Employer's organization or designated by their representative to oversee various aspects of construction projects. The primary responsibilities include overseeing maintenance activities, directing the Contractor on record-keeping requirements, ensuring compliance with regulations, and certifying work executed according to contractual obligations.

The Maintenance Surveyor has extensive authority over site operations, including issuing instructions through a Representative, approving or withholding permission for constructional plant on-site, making corrections or modifications in previous certificates, and issuing Variation Orders. They are also responsible for evaluating disputes, damages, and costs related to the project, certifying payments for work executed by both the Employer's workmen and other contractors, and overseeing final tests.

The Maintenance Surveyor is involved in managing claims from the Contractor, approving drawings as per contract terms, providing certificates of completion, and ensuring that all works are executed according to agreed specifications. They have authority over sub-contractors, can approve or prohibit their sub-letting, and clarify ambiguities between contract documents. Additionally, they oversee site inspections, approvals for tests and access to sites, and ensure compliance with contractual requirements.

The Maintenance Surveyor is also responsible for certifying the value of work executed on Complaint Chits submitted for payment, issuing orders related to maintenance and defects during the project (including suspension or requiring maintenance from the Contractor), receiving injury notifications from the Contractor, and providing instructions regarding removal or use of materials. They can consent or withhold permission for constructional plant on-site and are involved in agreements related to hiring or purchasing equipment.

In cases where there is ambiguity or discrepancy between contract documents, the Maintenance Surveyor has authority to interpret these terms and resolve such issues, ensuring clear communication and consistent application of contractual provisions. The role involves issuing orders related to variations and valuing them according to specified rules, examining proposals, approving drawings, surveying maintenance activities, managing progress, delays, and extensions related to work orders.

Overall, the Maintenance Surveyor plays a critical role in maintaining project integrity by ensuring that all aspects of construction are carried out as per contractual agreements.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02dce26d755dbc2a1f010f8cd0550db&lt;SEP&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b57445949baa2153e0f9f67f999456b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba22dc0a0fc19429a484bb41c261d34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c2d16f0534b8f7a9f0c286e3e24591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3e48c641bb7544fa8f59eeacc0c3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa9c6366e076e445101d83858797035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d72604c877ec1b265cace0cc38e4690d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1ba1c6b232e9a68005845d332fa7552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671cf14fabde451a853f4cb49e6a812f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62865738eafa658463c1c26212a98b20</data>
