<node id="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">A Works Order is an official document that authorizes and specifies the works to be executed by the Contractor under a contract. It details specific construction or maintenance tasks with prescribed timeframes, value estimates, and requirements for completion. The document may include verbal confirmations, complaints chits if their value does not exceed certain limits, and instructions from the Maintenance Surveyor regarding sequence, method, timing, or ingress/egress details of project execution.

Works Orders are part of a broader contract that outlines tasks to be completed by the Contractor, subject to measurement and variation procedures. They can include both verbal confirmations and complaints chits if their value does not exceed specified limits. The completion of Works Orders involves returning all provided documents (except contractor’s signed copies) to the Maintenance Surveyor.

Works Orders may require review or decision-making from the Maintenance Surveyor for certain details, such as changes in sequence, method, timing, or ingress/egress. They are sorted by the Maintenance Surveyor according to their claimed value into batches for further processing and can involve payment certificates issued after completion of specific tasks or projects.

In summary, a Works Order is an essential document within a contract that authorizes and details specific works to be executed by the Contractor with prescribed timelines, values, and requirements. It may include various types of instructions and confirmations from the Maintenance Surveyor and undergo review processes before finalization.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b57445949baa2153e0f9f67f999456b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c2d16f0534b8f7a9f0c286e3e24591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1ba1c6b232e9a68005845d332fa7552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62865738eafa658463c1c26212a98b20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671cf14fabde451a853f4cb49e6a812f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 34}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">The Contractor is a party involved in executing works under a construction contract. This entity is primarily responsible for carrying out work according to specified terms, conditions, and instructions from the Maintenance Surveyor or Employer. The Contractor must comply with various enactments and regulations on-site and ensure safety measures are in place. They may be required to submit detailed documents such as dimension books, bills of quantities, and supporting statements.

The Contractor is also responsible for executing works orders, making claims based on certain conditions, and potentially entering into sub-contracts or facing additional expenditures due to contract terms. They must adhere to specific obligations related to measurements, payments, and compliance with clauses in the contract. The Contractor may be required to provide materials, constructional plant, temporary buildings, and labor as part of their work.

In cases where delays occur, the Contractor is responsible for notifying the Maintenance Surveyor about such issues. Additionally, they are liable for executing works that require permanent reinstatement or maintenance obligations. The Contractor must ensure proper setting-out, rectify errors, provide emergency staff when necessary, and maintain site cleanliness after completing tasks.

The Contractor may be entitled to payment for work destroyed or damaged due to special risks but is also responsible for any non-compliant material or workmanship issues that arise during execution of the contract. They are required to submit various documents such as time worked, materials used, and priced statements on a daywork basis and must satisfy themselves regarding tender terms before submitting their bid.

In summary, the Contractor plays a crucial role in executing works under a construction contract, ensuring compliance with regulations, adhering to specific obligations, managing site operations safely, and maintaining records for claims or disputes.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d02dce26d755dbc2a1f010f8cd0550db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b57445949baa2153e0f9f67f999456b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba22dc0a0fc19429a484bb41c261d34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c2d16f0534b8f7a9f0c286e3e24591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8130c8086938f6df2