  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The subcontract APEX-2026-SUB-MEP-01 is derived from and references the main contract HDIL-2026-MC-01 for the Kowloon Bay Data Centre Project."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1cb1c6b428ba5b83e35bfc82ae647386</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HDIL-2026-MC-01&quot;" target="&quot;KOWLOON BAY DATA CENTRE PROJECT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"The project is specifically mentioned in HDIL-2026-MC-01, the main contract agreement between Harbourfront Data Infrastructure Limited and Apex Builders (HK) Limited."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAIN CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">19.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAIN CONTRACTOR is obligated to pay Liquidated Damages to the EMPLOYER if Practical Completion is not achieved by the deadline, and the EMPLOYER will make payments based on a fixed Lump Sum Contract Price of HK$48,000,000."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Main Contractor (Apex Builders (HK) Limited) is responsible to the Employer (Harbourfront Data Infrastructure Limited). "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-754aa01b6700b16ce9dfa955549688dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e1439fe1d96e82c71e1322be4ffbefc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAIN CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;LIQUIDATED DAMAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAIN CONTRACTOR is required to pay LIQUIDATED DAMAGES if Practical Completion is not achieved by the deadline specified (30 November 2027). The rate of Liquidated Damages is HK$50,000 per calendar day."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-754aa01b6700b16ce9dfa955549688dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAIN CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;SUBCONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">56.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAIN CONTRACTOR is responsible for paying the SUBCONTRACTOR under strict conditions, and also holds a PERFORMANCE BOND from the SUBCONTRACTOR."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Main Contractor and Subcontractor have a contractual relationship where the latter is responsible for providing services under subcontract works."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Subcontractor can submit written notices up to twenty-eight (28) calendar days after the end of the monthly payment cycle without any forfeiture or time-bar under Clause 7.3 of Cap. 57 or Cap. 282."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Subcontractor has the unconditional right to sub-let MEP installation works directly to third-party tier-2 sub-subcontractors without needing prior consent from the Main Contractor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Subcontractor has the unconditional right to sub-let up to 100% of MEP installation works without prior consent from, or notice to, the Main Contractor or Employer under Clause 9.2."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Subcontractor is permitted to supply and install certified refurbished chillers or OEM-equivalent switchgear manufactured in Mainland China or Southeast Asia, with legal and beneficial title remaining vested until full payment of the Final Account under Clause 8.1."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Subcontractor must submit a written Notice of Variation Claim within seven (7) calendar days to avoid permanent bar and extinguishment of the right to additional payment under Cap. 57 or Cap. 282."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6f34cc8c71a86a28ce1e2196a0e32a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4731062418096ba3a1831a12093dc972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c69babc4008d2fc0d3e203e2eb49977b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62cee928581076993e6dc7290419d468</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAIN CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;PERFORMANCE BOND&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAIN CONTRACTOR holds a PERFORMANCE BOND from the SUBCONTRACTOR, which will be released upon expiry of the Defects Liability Period."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Main Contractor retains the Performance Bond until the end of the extended defect rectification period, indicating a financial responsibility and oversight role."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6f34cc8c71a86a28ce1e2196a0e32a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c69babc4008d2fc0d3e203e2eb49977b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAIN CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;SUBCONTRACTOR'S WORKERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">12.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Subcontractor is responsible for maintaining a qualified site supervisor as per Clause 9.1 of Cap. 57 or Cap. 282."&lt;SEP&gt;"Workers can make claims against the Main Contractor under Cap. 57 or Cap. 282 if injured or unpaid."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4731062418096ba3a1831a12093dc972</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIQUIDATED DAMAGES&quot;" target="&quot;PRACTICAL COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The LIQUIDATED DAMAGES are triggered if the PRACTICAL COMPLETION is not achieved by 30 November 2027. The rate of Liquidated Damages is HK$50,000 per calendar day."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-754aa01b6700b16ce9dfa955549688dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIQUIDATED DAMAGES&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT RESPONSE AND SETTLEMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">24.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer's Engineer must issue a Payment Response and make payments within 45 days after receipt of a PAYMENT CLAIM. If Practical Completion is not achieved by the deadline, LIQUIDATED DAMAGES will be triggered at HK$50,000 per calendar day."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer's Engineer must issue a Payment Response and make payments within 90 days after the date of the PAYMENT CLAIM. If Practical Completion is not achieved by the deadline, LIQUIDATED DAMAGES will be triggered at HK$50,000 per calendar day."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-754aa01b6700b16ce9dfa955549688dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIQUIDATED DAMAGES&quot;" target="&quot;DELAY PENALTIES AND FORFEITURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Delay Penalties involve payment at a fixed rate per working day if Practical Completion is not achieved by the deadline, while Liquidated Damages are part of this clause specifying the penalty amount."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c8960d3af997dd63f6f6d7ffacd99c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIQUIDATED DAMAGES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LIQUIDATED DAMAGES can be claimed from the CONTRACTOR by the EMPLOYER if the Contractor fails to complete works as per the Contract or causes delays, with additional costs recoverable for emergency work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIQUIDATED DAMAGES&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER has the right to claim LIQUIDATED DAMAGES from the CONTRACTOR for non-compliance with contractual obligations and delays in work completion or emergency response."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT_A_MAIN_WORKS_AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;HK$48,000,000 (HONG KONG DOLLARS FORTY-EIGHT MILLION ONLY)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The fixed Lump Sum Contract Price of HK$48,000,000 is the total amount agreed upon in the CONTRACT_A_MAIN_WORKS_AGREEMENT for the Main Contractor to complete their work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-754aa01b6700b16ce9dfa955549688dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT_A_MAIN_WORKS_AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;SERVICE OF PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Service of Process is defined in the CONTRACT_A_MAIN_WORKS_AGREEMENT, specifying how legal notices should be served."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ad2a4a96d27752f49d1fe3251581e042</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT_A_MAIN_WORKS_AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MANDATORY HKIAC ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Mandatory HKIAC Arbitration as per the CONTRACT_A_MAIN_WORKS_AGREEMENT dictates that any disputes must be resolved by arbitration administered by HKIAC."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ad2a4a96d27752f49d1fe3251581e042</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT_A_MAIN_WORKS_AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;PRICING AND PAYMENT SCHEDULE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PRICING AND PAYMENT SCHEDULE is part of the CONTRACT_A_MAIN_WORKS_AGREEMENT, detailing the contract price and payment terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ad2a4a96d27752f49d1fe3251581e042</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRACTICAL COMPLETION&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT CLAIM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAIN CONTRACTOR must submit PAYMENT CLAIMs to ensure timely payment for work completed towards PRACTICAL COMPLETION. Failure to achieve Practical Completion by the deadline will result in Liquidated Damages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-754aa01b6700b16ce9dfa955549688dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRACTICAL COMPLETION&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT RESPONSE AND SETTLEMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer's Engineer must issue a Payment Response and make payments within 45 days after receipt of a PAYMENT CLAIM. If Practical Completion is not achieved by the deadline, LIQUIDATED DAMAGES will be triggered at HK$50,000 per calendar day."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer's Engineer must issue a Payment Response and make payments within 90 days after the date of the PAYMENT CLAIM. If Practical Completion is not achieved by the deadline, LIQUIDATED DAMAGES will be triggered at HK$50,000 per calendar day."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-754aa01b6700b16ce9dfa955549688dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PRACTICAL COMPLETION&quot;" target="&quot;SUBCONTRACT WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Subcontract Works are related to Practical Completion as the obligations under Subcontract Works cease upon its expiry."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c69babc4008d2fc0d3e203e2eb49977b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HK$48,000,000 (HONG KONG DOLLARS FORTY-EIGHT MILLION ONLY)&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT RESPONSE AND SETTLEMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer's Engineer must issue a Payment Response and make payments within 90 days after the date of the PAYMENT CLAIM. The total CONTRACT SUM is HK$48,000,000."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-754aa01b6700b16ce9dfa955549688dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RETENTION MONEY&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT CLAIM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAIN CONTRACTOR submits monthly interim payment claims on the last day of each month. The Employer will deduct RETENTION MONEY at a rate of five percent (5%) from these payments, with a maximum Limit of Retention of HK$1,500,000."&lt;SEP&gt;"The RETENTION MONEY of 5% from each interim payment will be deducted based on PAYMENT CLAIMs submitted by the MAIN CONTRACTOR. The Employer's Engineer must issue a Payment Response within 45 days after receipt, and payments are due within 90 days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-754aa01b6700b16ce9dfa955549688dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RETENTION MONEY&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT RESPONSE AND SETTLEMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">21.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer's Engineer must issue a Payment Response and make payments within 90 days after the date of the PAYMENT CLAIM. RETENTION MONEY is deducted at the rate of five percent (5%) from each interim payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer's Engineer must issue a Payment Response within 45 days after receipt of a PAYMENT CLAIM, and payments are due within 90 days. RETENTION MONEY is deducted at the rate of five percent (5%) from each interim payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-754aa01b6700b16ce9dfa955549688dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PAYMENT CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT RESPONSE AND SETTLEMENT PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PAYMENT RESPONSE AND SETTLEMENT PERIOD requires the Employer's Engineer to issue a Payment Response within 45 calendar days after receipt of a PAYMENT CLAIM, and payments are due within 90 days after the date of the Payment Claim."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-754aa01b6700b16ce9dfa955549688dc</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILLERS, UNINTERRUPTIBLE POWER SUPPLIES (UPS), AND HIGH-VOLTAGE SWITCHGEAR&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS AND MATERIALS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"These are all types of equipment and materials used in construction projects."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILLERS, UNINTERRUPTIBLE POWER SUPPLIES (UPS), AND HIGH-VOLTAGE SWITCHGEAR&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"All these items fall under the broader category of Constructional Plant."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILLERS, UNINTERRUPTIBLE POWER SUPPLIES (UPS), AND HIGH-VOLTAGE SWITCHGEAR&quot;" target="&quot;PLANT USAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Plant Usage includes the utilization of machinery, equipment, and other tools necessary for site operations that are recorded daily in Site Diaries. These include chillers, uninterruptible power supplies, and high-voltage switchgear as part of ongoing maintenance or construction activities."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILLERS, UNINTERRUPTIBLE POWER SUPPLIES (UPS), AND HIGH-VOLTAGE SWITCHGEAR&quot;" target="&quot;ACCESS TO THE SITE AND PLACES OF MANUFACTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Access refers to permissions granted for entry into specific areas, including manufacturing sites, necessary for material supply or inspection purposes. This is relevant as these are types of equipment that must be brand-new and manufactured in the European Union or Japan."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILLERS, UNINTERRUPTIBLE POWER SUPPLIES (UPS), AND HIGH-VOLTAGE SWITCHGEAR&quot;" target="&quot;GOVERNMENT OFFICER / COMPANY NAME&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"The government officer/company name might be involved in the procurement or regulation of these products."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY SECURITY OF PAYMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 652)&quot;" target="&quot;CHILLERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance applies to the payment terms for chillers installed under the Works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY SECURITY OF PAYMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 652)&quot;" target="&quot;UNINTERRUPTIBLE POWER SUPPLIES (UPS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance applies to the payment terms for uninterruptible power supplies installed under the Works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY SECURITY OF PAYMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 652)&quot;" target="&quot;HIGH-VOLTAGE SWITCHGEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance applies to the payment terms for high-voltage switchgear installed under the Works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY SECURITY OF PAYMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 652)&quot;" target="&quot;PROJECT SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance governs payment terms and other aspects related to the project site, including title passing and working hours."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY SECURITY OF PAYMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 652)&quot;" target="&quot;NIGHT SHIFTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance regulates work schedules on the project site, including restrictions on night shifts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY SECURITY OF PAYMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 652)&quot;" target="&quot;DEFECTS LIABILITY PERIOD (DLP)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Defects Liability Period is a term defined under the Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY SECURITY OF PAYMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 652)&quot;" target="&quot;DATE OF PRACTICAL COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Date of Practical Completion marks the start of the Defects Liability Period as per the Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY SECURITY OF PAYMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 652)&quot;" target="&quot;CHILLERS, UNINTERRUPTIBLE POWER SUPPLIES (UPS), HIGH-VOLTAGE SWITCHGEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance governs the payment and quality standards for all MEP systems installed under the Works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY SECURITY OF PAYMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 652)&quot;" target="&quot;NIGHT SHIFTS, DATE OF PRACTICAL COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance regulates work schedules and practical completion dates on the project site."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY SECURITY OF PAYMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 652)&quot;" target="&quot;CHILLERS, UNINTERRUPTIBLE POWER SUPPLIES (UPS), HIGH-VOLTAGE SWITCHGEAR, NIGHT SHIFTS, DEFECTS LIABILITY PERIOD (DLP), DATE OF PRACTICAL COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance governs the payment terms and quality standards for all MEP systems installed under the Works as well as work schedules and defects liability period on the project site."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY SECURITY OF PAYMENT ORDINANCE (CAP. 652)&quot;" target="&quot;MAIN CONTRACTOR'S ENTITLEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAIN CONTRACTOR's entitlement to payment from the EMPLOYER is subject to compliance with the CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY SECURITY OF PAYMENT ORDINANCE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6f34cc8c71a86a28ce1e2196a0e32a1a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILLERS&quot;" target="&quot;UNINTERRUPTIBLE POWER SUPPLIES (UPS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both chillers and uninterruptible power supplies are types of equipment that must be brand-new, manufactured in specific regions as per quality standards outlined by the Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILLERS&quot;" target="&quot;HIGH-VOLTAGE SWITCHGEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"All three pieces of equipment—chillers, uninterruptible power supplies (UPS), and high-voltage switchgear—are mentioned in the same quality standards section under the Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHILLERS&quot;" target="&quot;DEFECTS LIABILITY PERIOD (DLP)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Defects Liability Period applies to all MEP systems installed under the Works, which includes chillers as per the Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNINTERRUPTIBLE POWER SUPPLIES (UPS)&quot;" target="&quot;HIGH-VOLTAGE SWITCHGEAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both uninterruptible power supplies and high-voltage switchgear are types of equipment that must be brand-new, manufactured in specific regions as per quality standards outlined by the Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNINTERRUPTIBLE POWER SUPPLIES (UPS)&quot;" target="&quot;DEFECTS LIABILITY PERIOD (DLP)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Defects Liability Period applies to all MEP systems installed under the Works, which includes uninterruptible power supplies as per the Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HIGH-VOLTAGE SWITCHGEAR&quot;" target="&quot;DEFECTS LIABILITY PERIOD (DLP)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Defects Liability Period applies to all MEP systems installed under the Works, which includes high-voltage switchgear as per the Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROJECT SITE&quot;" target="&quot;NIGHT SHIFTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Night shifts are strictly prohibited on the project site due to adjacent commercial tenant operations and Noise Control Ordinance restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROJECT SITE&quot;" target="&quot;DEFECTS LIABILITY PERIOD (DLP)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Defects Liability Period applies to any defects that may arise on the project site after practical completion as per the Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROJECT SITE&quot;" target="&quot;INDEMNITY FOR CRIMINAL PENALTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Indemnity for Criminal Penalties covers the Employer’s liability to pay criminal fines or statutory penalties imposed on them due to negligence of any person, including those related to Project Site safety and health regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c8960d3af997dd63f6f6d7ffacd99c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFECTS LIABILITY PERIOD (DLP)&quot;" target="&quot;DATE OF PRACTICAL COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Defects Liability Period for all works, including MEP systems, starts from the Date of Practical Completion as per the Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFECTS LIABILITY PERIOD (DLP)&quot;" target="&quot;PROJECT SITE, NIGHT SHIFTS, DATE OF PRACTICAL COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"All aspects related to defects liability period are interconnected with the project site, night shifts restrictions and practical completion date as per the Construction Industry Security of Payment Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3b058c3b28ea06cde28836452c1e618</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFECTS LIABILITY PERIOD (DLP)&quot;" target="&quot;SUBCONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SUBCONTRACTOR has a 12-Month Defects Liability Period during which they are responsible for rectifying defects in their work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-6f34cc8c71a86a28ce1e2196a0e32a1a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER LIABILITY CAP&quot;" target="&quot;INDEMNITY FOR CRIMINAL PENALTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both clauses deal with financial responsibilities of the Employer under different scenarios, specifically criminal penalties and liability for personal injury on Project Site."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c8960d3af997dd63f6f6d7ffacd99c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RESTRICTION ON SUB-SUBCONTRACTING&quot;" target="&quot;DOMESTIC MEP SUBCONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Restriction on Sub-Subcontracting allows engagement of a domestic MEP subcontractor but prohibits further subletting to tier-2 without Employer's consent, impacting the Domestic MEP Subcontractor’s role and responsibilities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c8960d3af997dd63f6f6d7ffacd99c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION MECHANISM&quot;" target="&quot;EXCLUSIVE COURT JURISDICTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dispute Resolution Mechanism includes Exclusive Court Jurisdiction clause specifying that Hong Kong courts have exclusive jurisdiction over any disputes arising from the contract, impacting how disputes are resolved and where they can be heard."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c8960d3af997dd63f6f6d7ffacd99c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE RESOLUTION MECHANISM&quot;" target="&quot;HKIAC ARBITRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"While not explicitly mentioned in the text, HKIAC (Hong Kong International Arbitration Centre) is a common alternative to court jurisdiction for dispute resolution mechanisms. The absence of arbitration as an option here suggests it's excluded by Exclusive Court Jurisdiction clause."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c8960d3af997dd63f6f6d7ffacd99c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
