<edge source="&quot;GOVERNMENT OF HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The GOVERNMENT OF HONG KONG appoints and oversees the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR in executing contract obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOVERNMENT OF HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The GOVERNMENT OF HONG KONG also oversees the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE who acts under their authority."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GOVERNMENT OF HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer in this context refers to the Government of Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON OR PERSONS APPOINTED FROM TIME TO TIME BY MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR AND NOTIFIED TO CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor's Representative performs duties set forth by the Surveyor, as communicated in writing to the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">53.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Maintenance Surveyor's Representative is appointed to perform duties set forth by the Maintenance Surveyor, interacting with and instructing the Contractor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CONTRACTOR must take instructions only from the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR or his REpresentative as per Clause (2)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contractor is required to provide daily work records and statements to the Maintenance Surveyor's Representative for daywork activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contractor must receive written instructions or approvals from the Maintenance Surveyor's Representative within the terms of any delegation for them to bind the Contractor and Employer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor's Representative shares similar authority with the Maintenance Surveyor to access sites, examine work before covering up, direct uncovering or making openings in the Works, and order removal of unsatisfactory material."&lt;SEP&gt;"The representative can give written instructions that bind the Contractor, which require approval from the Employer in terms of assignments and sub-lets. The Maintenance Surveyor must act with the consent of the Employer for certain actions to be valid."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2f5b22ce699e51609625c61aad79755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE has the authority to give instructions and approvals related to WORKS ORDERS within delegated powers from the Maintenance Surveyor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR's Representative countersigns WORKS ORDERS to acceptably carried out work, which is necessary for payment claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor has the authority to delegate duties and powers to their representative, who can give written instructions binding on the Contractor with certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The representative signs the Complaint Chit to acceptably carry out work within 12 working days of issue, acting on behalf of the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR'S ASSIGNMENT OR SUB-LETTING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">31.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The representative can give written instructions that bind the Contractor and Employer in relation to assignments and sub-lets. The Maintenance Surveyor must act with the consent of the Employer for certain actions to be valid."&lt;SEP&gt;"The representative can give written instructions that bind the Contractor and Employer, affecting their ability to assign or sub-let without proper delegation from the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">32.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The representative can give written instructions that bind the Contractor, which require approval from the Employer in terms of assignments and sub-lets. The Maintenance Surveyor must act with the consent of the Employer for certain actions to be valid."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;AUTHORIZED ENGLISH-SPEAKING AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE gives directions to the AUTHORIZED ENGLISH-SPEAKING AGENT on behalf of the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;THE CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">16.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is required to comply with directives from and provide information to the Maintenance Surveyor's Representative."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contractor is required to deliver daily returns to the Maintenance Surveyor's Representative as per their records on labor, materials, etc."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3e48c641bb7544fa8f59eeacc0c3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;SITE DIARY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor's Representative maintains a Site Diary that records various aspects related to the Works and labor on-site."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;LABOR RETURNS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor's Representative receives Labor Returns from the Contractor, which are used in maintaining the Site Diary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor's Representative ensures compliance with enactments, regulations, and by-laws applicable to the Works on behalf of the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC BODIES AND COMPANIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor's Representative must ensure compliance with the rules and regulations of public bodies and companies involved in the Works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;INDUSTRIES INVOLVED&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor's Representative oversees the Works in industries that are subject to specific regulatory requirements and compliance verification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor's Representative is responsible for checking the progress of the works and approving expenditures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor's Representative is responsible for overseeing and documenting the progress and quality of the Works on-site."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;THE EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Representative acts on behalf of the Employer to manage and oversee the Contractor’s activities at the site, ensuring compliance with their policies regarding discoveries like fossils."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3e48c641bb7544fa8f59eeacc0c3c2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (A)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-clause A grants authority to Maintenance Surveyor's Representative for ordering examinations, measurements or tests."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE [GCCBWT] 45&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-clause GCCBWT 45 also grants access to the Maintenance Surveyor's Representative on-site."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;CLAUSE 51&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause 51 sets a time frame for completion of works, which affects when necessary instructions are provided by the Maintenance Surveyor's Representative."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR’S PROPOSED DAYWORK ACTIVITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor's Representative must approve or check the Contractor’s proposed daywork activities before reimbursement can be made."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;COMPLAINT CHIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR's Representative countersigns COMPLAINT CHITS to acceptably carried out work, which is necessary for payment claims within 12 working days of issue."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;DIMENSION BOOK(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"When submitted with dimensions endorsed by CONTRACTOR on COMPLAINT CHITs or attached WORKS ORDERS, DIMENSION BOOK(S) are required to be accompanied by supporting documents as determined by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ASSIGNMENT&quot;" target="&quot;SUBLETTING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"ASSIGNMENT and SUBLETTING are related as both involve transferring rights or obligations from one party to another in a contract context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT DOCUMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;DRAWINGS PROVIDED BY THE CONTRACTOR FOR THE WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The DRAWINGS provided by the Contractor for the Works are part of the broader CONTRACT DOCUMENTS that define work scope and requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT DOCUMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;CLAUSE 64&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLAUSE 64 is part of the CONTRACT DOCUMENTS, providing guidance on dealing with ambiguities and discrepancies in costs."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT DOCUMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;DRAWINGS PROVIDED BY THE CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CONTRACT DOCUMENTS include DRAWINGS provided by the CONTRACTOR, and these drawings need approval from the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT DOCUMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;INFORMATION NOT TO BE DIVULGED&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Information in CONTRACT DOCUMENTS is not to be divulged, including those from the EMPLOYER or MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR provided through these documents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT DOCUMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLES OF AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The ARTICLES OF AGREEMENT are prepared at the expense of the EMPLOYER, using CONTRACT DOCUMENTS and other provided documents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT DOCUMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;DRAWINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DRAWINGS or other documents provided by the CONTRACTOR form part of the CONTRACT DOCUMENTS which must be in English as per Clause 9."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTOR'S EMPLOYEES&quot;" target="&quot;EMERGENCY STAFF&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both CONSTRUCTOR'S EMPLOYEES and EMERGENCY STAFF are involved in site operations, with EMERGENCY STAFF providing additional support during emergencies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY STAFF&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for having EMERGENCY STAFF available at all times to execute necessary tasks during emergencies, as per general guidelines provided in the text."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SETTING-OUT&quot;" target="&quot;SAFETY AND SECURITY OF THE WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"SETTING-OUT is crucial for SAFETY AND SECURITY OF THE WORKS as it ensures proper layout and positioning of the construction site, reducing risks to personnel and property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SETTING-OUT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR’S RESPONSIBILITY FOR STABILITY AND SAFETY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is responsible for ensuring that setting-out is correct and true, which includes protecting and preserving bench-marks, site-rails, pegs, etc."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SAFETY AND SECURITY OF THE WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;DAMAGE TO PERSONS AND PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Safety and security measures are in place to prevent DAMAGE TO PERSONS AND PROPERTY during construction activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAMAGE TO PERSONS AND PROPERTY&quot;" target="&quot;OUTBREAK OF WAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An outbreak of war could lead to significant damage to persons and property in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAMAGE TO PERSONS AND PROPERTY&quot;" target="&quot;INVASION OF HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The invasion of Hong Kong would likely result in damage to persons and property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAMAGE TO PERSONS AND PROPERTY&quot;" target="&quot;ACT OF FOREIGN TERRORISTS IN HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Acts by foreign terrorists could cause injury or damage to people and property in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAMAGE TO PERSONS AND PROPERTY&quot;" target="&quot;CIVIL WAR, REBELLION, REVOLUTION OR MILITARY OR USURPED POWER IN HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A civil war or similar conflict would likely result in significant damage to persons and property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAMAGE TO PERSONS AND PROPERTY&quot;" target="&quot;RIOT, COMMOTION OR DISORDER IN HONG KONG&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Riots or disorder could lead to injury or damage to people and property in Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAMAGE TO PERSONS AND PROPERTY&quot;" target="&quot;OCCUPATION BY EMPLOYER'S AGENTS, EMPLOYEES, TENANTS OR OTHER CONTRACTORS NOT EMPLOYED BY CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Occupation by unauthorized parties could result in damage to persons and property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAMAGE TO PERSONS AND PROPERTY&quot;" target="&quot;MAKING GOOD OF PROPERTY DAMAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Damage to persons and property may require making good of any property damage as a result of the execution of works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DESIGN RESPONSIBILITY&quot;" target="&quot;INTERFERENCE WITH TRAFFIC AND ADJOINING PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DESIGN RESPONSIBILITY includes considerations for INTERFERENCE with traffic and adjoining properties, ensuring that the design minimizes negative impacts on surrounding areas."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REMEDY ON FAILURE TO INSURE&quot;" target="&quot;ACCIDENT OR INJURY TO WORKMEN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In case of ACCIDENT or INJURY to WORKMEN due to failure to insure, REMEDY is required as per the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACCIDENT OR INJURY TO WORKMEN&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR TO GIVE NOTICE OF INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR must give notice of any ACCIDENT or INJURY to WORKMEN, ensuring timely response and documentation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACCIDENT OR INJURY TO WORKMEN&quot;" target="&quot;ENGAGEMENT OF LABOUR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The engagement of labour is related to the potential for accidents or injuries among workmen."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACCIDENT OR INJURY TO WORKMEN&quot;" target="&quot;FAIR WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fair wages may impact the safety culture and reduce incidents, indirectly relating to accident prevention."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATENT RIGHTS AND ROYALTIES&quot;" target="&quot;NOTICES TO BE WRITTEN IN ENGLISH AND CHINESE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Patent rights and royalties may involve NOTICES that need to be written in both English and Chinese as per the contract requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATENT RIGHTS AND ROYALTIES&quot;" target="&quot;EXECUTION OF WORK OF REPAIR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Patent rights and royalties may be involved in the legal aspects of executing work repairs, especially if new technologies are used."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATENT RIGHTS AND ROYALTIES&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS AND MATERIALS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant may include items that have patent rights."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATENT RIGHTS AND ROYALTIES&quot;" target="&quot;ROYALTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Royalties are payments made by the Contractor to owners of intellectual property rights in relation to the use or sale of their inventions or technologies used in construction works."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE DIARY AND LABOUR RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;CLEARANCE OF THE SITE ON COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SITE DIARY and Labour Returns are used for CLEARANCE of the site on completion, documenting work progress and compliance with contractual obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE DIARY AND LABOUR RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;FOSSILS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"FOSSILS found during construction may be recorded in the SITE DIARY AND LABOUR RETURNS as part of project documentation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE DIARY AND LABOUR RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLICATION OF PHOTOGRAPHS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Photographs published may be documented in SITE DIARY AND LABOUR RETURNS as part of project records and compliance with contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE DIARY AND LABOUR RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The contractor is responsible for maintaining site diary and labour returns as part of their duties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE DIARY AND LABOUR RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;RATE OF PROGRESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Site diary and labour returns provide data for monitoring the rate of progress on site."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE DIARY AND LABOUR RETURNS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Site Diary and Labor Returns are documents used for recording daily activities, labor hours, and other relevant information on a construction site under the supervision of the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FOSSILS&quot;" target="&quot;UNCOVERING AND MAKING OPENINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fossils may be encountered during uncovering and making openings, requiring special handling or documentation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FACILITIES FOR OTHER CONTRACTORS&quot;" target="&quot;CLEARANCE OF THE SITE ON COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Facilities for other contractors contribute to a smooth CLEARANCE of the site on completion, ensuring all parties' needs are met during final stages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2575de447c966aae5e5a22feec1323</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLEARANCE OF THE SITE ON COMPLETION&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLICATION OF PHOTOGRAPHS OF THE SITE OR THE WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clearance of the site involves ensuring all work is complete before publication of photographs for record-keeping and marketing purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLICATION OF PHOTOGRAPHS OF THE SITE OR THE WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SITE's condition is subject to photographic documentation with permission from the EMPLOYER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENGAGEMENT OF LABOUR&quot;" target="&quot;FAIR WAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Fair wages are a key factor in engaging labour effectively on construction sites."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENGAGEMENT OF LABOUR&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR must engage labour in Hong Kong and provide fair wages, adhering to local usage and government regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;QUALITY OF MATERIALS AND WORKMANSHIP AND TESTS&quot;" target="&quot;ACCESS TO THE SITE AND PLACES OF MANUFACTURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Quality of materials and workmanship tests require access to the site and places of manufacture for inspection."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;QUALITY OF MATERIALS AND WORKMANSHIP AND TESTS&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS AND MATERIALS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Quality is a critical aspect when dealing with Constructional Plant."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ACCESS TO THE SITE AND PLACES OF MANUFACTURE&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS AND MATERIALS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant often requires access to various sites."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNCOVERING AND MAKING OPENINGS&quot;" target="&quot;EXAMINATION OF WORK BEFORE COVERING UP&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Examination before covering up is necessary after making openings to ensure proper construction practices are followed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RATE OF PROGRESS&quot;" target="&quot;LIQUIDATED DAMAGES FOR DELAY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rate of progress affects the risk and potential for liquidated damages if delays occur in completing work on time."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RATE OF PROGRESS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rate of progress concerns how quickly the CONTRACTOR completes their work, and may impact further actions by MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-671cf14fabde451a853f4cb49e6a812f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RATE OF PROGRESS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor monitors the rate of progress to ensure work is being completed at an acceptable pace, issuing instructions for expedited progress if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIQUIDATED DAMAGES FOR DELAY&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer can claim liquidated damages from the Contractor if work is not completed on time."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-671cf14fabde451a853f4cb49e6a812f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LIQUIDATED DAMAGES FOR DELAY&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"LIQUIDATED DAMAGES FOR DELAY are calculated based on the estimated value of the WORKS ORDER and the prescribed completion time, to be paid by the CONTRACTOR if not completed within that timeframe."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liquidated damages are related to WORKS ORDER completion deadlines; failure to meet these can result in payment of liquidated damages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-671cf14fabde451a853f4cb49e6a812f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUSPENSION OF THE WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE AND DEFECTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Suspension can lead to maintenance issues or defects that need addressing upon resumption of works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXECUTION OF WORK OF REPAIR&quot;" target="&quot;VESTING OF CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT AND TEMPORARY BUILDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Execution of work repairs may involve the use and management of constructional plant and temporary buildings."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VESTING OF CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT AND TEMPORARY BUILDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS AND MATERIALS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant is often involved in vesting processes."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOMINATED SUBCONTRACTORS&quot;" target="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS AND MATERIALS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Nominated subcontractors are involved in the procurement and handling of constructional plant, temporary buildings, and materials."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9df361e92365fbde2d17501741344b9a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS AND MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;HIRED AND HIRE-PURCHASE CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT 27&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant includes items like hire-purchase equipment."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS AND MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;PROVISION OF INSTRUMENTS FOR SETTING-OUT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant often includes instruments for setting-out."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS AND MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;TONNAGE ROYALTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant often involves tonnage-related payments."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS AND MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;ROYALTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant may include items with associated royalties."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS AND MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;RENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant often involves rental arrangements."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS AND MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;WORK CARRIED OUT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant is often used in work carried out."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS AND MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;LABOR ON-SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant often requires labor for its use."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS AND MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;PLANT USAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant is often used in plant usage."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR OR HIS REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor or his representative certifies the completion of a Works Order."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR OR HIS REPRESENTATIVE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor issues a certificate upon completing all parts of a Works Order."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;HIRED AND HIRE-PURCHASE CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT 27&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The hired or purchase construction plant falls within the broader category of constructional plant used in the works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;LIABILITY FOR LOSS OR DAMAGE TO CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT 28&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The constructional plant is subject to liability in case of loss or damage, which affects its usage and maintenance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;EXECUTION OF THE WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant includes appliances required for executing the Works but excludes materials forming part of permanent work or vehicles transporting personnel, etc."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT and TEMPORARY WORKS are part of the overall Works to be executed by the CONTRACTOR under the terms of the CONTRACT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is responsible for providing and maintaining lights, guards, fences, warning signs, and watchmen when necessary regarding Constructional Plant safety measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contractor must remove Constructional Plant from the Site upon contract termination."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d995518579c80996691b5d1b66c19ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;MACHINE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both are types of equipment required for the Works and subject to patent infringement clauses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has authority to oversee the removal or sale of CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT and can enforce actions against the CONTRACTOR if necessary."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor has consent power over bringing Constructional Plant onto the Site."&lt;SEP&gt;"The effect of Constructional Plant shortages or labor issues on work completion may be considered by the Maintenance Surveyor when deciding if a Contractor should receive an extension of time."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Nominated Sub-contractor's failure to provide Constructional Plant timely may affect work completion, impacting Contractor's extension claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;SUB-CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant usage may involve sub-contract agreements for its execution and maintenance by the contractor's subcontractors."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Employer acquires the right to use and potentially own certain Constructional Plant through agreements with contractors."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY BUILDINGS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant and Temporary Buildings are both brought upon the Site by the Contractor for use in construction activities."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS ORDER WITH AN ESTIMATED VALUE NOT EXCEEDING THE AMOUNT STATED IN THE APPENDIX TO THE FORM OF TENDER&quot;" target="&quot;COMPLAINT CHIT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Complaint Chit is essentially a type of Works Order that meets specific criteria regarding its value and form."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS ORDER ISSUED UNDER THE CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;COMPLETION OF A WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The completion of any single Works Order issued under the contract signifies progress on the overall project."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS ORDER ISSUED UNDER THE CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;COMPLETION OF THE WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Completing all issued Works Orders under the contract means that the entire project is completed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS ORDER ISSUED UNDER THE CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;INCORPORATION OF CERTAIN CLAUSES IN SUB-CONTRACTS 28&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Certain clauses related to works orders are incorporated into subcontracts as part of contract management."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;CORRECTION AND WITHHOLDING OF CERTIFICATES 30&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Certificates, including maintenance certificates, may require corrections or withholdings based on specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLES OF AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE CERTIFICATE is issued based on the performance outlined in ARTICLES OF AGREEMENT, indicating a direct relationship between them for completion of works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Works Order under the Contract leads to the issuance of a Maintenance Certificate upon completion and approval by the Maintenance Surveyor after the Maintenance Period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Period is crucial for determining when a final Maintenance Certificate can be issued, ensuring all work has been completed satisfactorily."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The maintenance certificate is issued by the Maintenance Surveyor to confirm that the Contractor has completed their obligations as per the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ba22dc0a0fc19429a484bb41c261d34</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor issues a certificate stating that all repair and reconstruction works have been completed satisfactorily."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORFEITURE&quot;" target="&quot;CLAUSE 53 OR CLAUSE 67&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clauses 53 or 67 are referenced in relation to claims that could lead to Forfeiture if not adhered to properly by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ba22dc0a0fc19429a484bb41c261d34</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORFEITURE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor's certification or actions can trigger the Forfeiture clause if certain conditions related to the Contractor's performance are not met."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ba22dc0a0fc19429a484bb41c261d34</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SETTLEMENT OF DISPUTES 33&quot;" target="&quot;DEFAULT OF THE EMPLOYER 35&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dispute settlement mechanisms may be invoked in cases where an employer defaults on their obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SERVICE OF NOTICES 34&quot;" target="&quot;NOTICES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The service of notices is a general term that includes various types of notifications required under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT provide the framework for claims made by the CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor is responsible for certifying completion, which triggers actions by the Contractor regarding site clearance after receiving this document."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3e48c641bb7544fa8f59eeacc0c3c2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION&quot;" target="&quot;THE CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Upon issuance of the Certificate of Completion, The Contractor must clear and remove all surplus materials from the Site as per Maintenance Surveyor's instructions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3e48c641bb7544fa8f59eeacc0c3c2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The issuance of a CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION obligates the CONTRACTOR to remove all CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS, and SURPLUS MATERIALS from the SITE as per CLAUSE 74."&lt;SEP&gt;"Upon issuance, the CONTRACTOR must clear the SITE as per the CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION is issued by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR after a WORKS ORDER has been substantially completed and passed final tests, signifying its completion."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Certificate of Completion can be issued for a final WORKS ORDER, though it is not a condition precedent to arbitration as per Clause 87(1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR issues a CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION at the end of the MAINTENANCE PERIOD, confirming work completion."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0c2d16f0534b8f7a9f0c286e3e24591</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The issuance of a CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION signifies that all WORKS are completed, triggering the obligations of the CONTRACTOR to remove CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT and TEMPORARY BUILDINGS from the SITE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPLAINT CHIT&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Complaint Chit is a specific type of Works Order with an estimated value not exceeding a certain amount."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPLAINT CHIT&quot;" target="&quot;DIMENSION BOOK(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The dimensions of work completed pursuant to a COMPLAINT CHIT should be endorsed on the reverse side or attached, indicating their importance in measurement and valuation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPLAINT CHIT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The COMPLAINT CHIT, when submitted with dimensions endorsed by CONTRACTOR, is used for payment claims. The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR may check and certify the value of work executed on it."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPLAINT CHIT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR checks COMPLAINT CHITS and may refer them back to the CONTRACTOR if details are not provided within 12 working days, then samples will be checked for payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPLETION OF A WORKS ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS 29&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interim payments can be made for the completion of individual Works Orders during project execution."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPLETION OF A WORKS ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The completion of a Works Order signifies the end of all tasks included in one particular Works Order."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMPLETION OF THE WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDERS ISSUED UNDER THE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Completion of the Works refers to the overall completion of all Works Orders that have been issued under the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HIRED AND HIRE-PURCHASE CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT 27&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER'S EXPENSE IN ENTERING INTO HIRE OR HIRE-PURCHASE AGREEMENT 28&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Expenses related to hiring or purchasing constructional plant are part of the employer’s financial obligations under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d04fd928cd5cdad2902f95e470d14ad3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLES OF AGREEMENT, TENDER AND ACCEPTANCE THEREOF BY THE EMPLOYER, DRAWINGS, GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT, SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT IF ANY, SPECIFICATION AND SCHEDULE OF RATES.&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contract encompasses various documents including Articles of Agreement, Tender, Drawings, etc."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;TENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The TENDER submitted by the CONTRACTOR forms part of the CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT and TEMPORARY WORKS AGREEMENT under the terms of the CONTRACT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-clause 2 specifies requirements for examinations, measurements or tests as per contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Works are governed by the terms of the Contract, including provisions for maintenance and defects."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The arbitrator has full power to review any decision made by the Maintenance Surveyor regarding the Contract unless it pertains specifically to Clause 48(3)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT AREA&quot;" target="&quot;AREA REFERRED TO IN THE CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contract Area specifies the geographical area covered by the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT AREA&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Inspection of the CONTRACT AREA is necessary for understanding the nature of work to be executed on the WORKS before submitting a tender by the CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COST&quot;" target="&quot;EXPENDITURE REASONABLY INCURRED INCLUDING OVERHEADS AND DEPRECIATION OF CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT OWNED BY THE CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Cost includes various expenditures related to executing Works, excluding profit."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DRAWINGS&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIFICATION OR SCHEDULE OF RATES AND ANY MODIFICATION APPROVED IN WRITING BY THE MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Drawings are part of the Specification or Schedule of Rates that may be modified with written approval from the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DRAWINGS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DRAWINGS are considered mutually explanatory with other documents and can be used by MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR for instructions on ambiguities or discrepancies."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor is responsible for issuing Drawings to the Contractor as needed during work execution."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b57445949baa2153e0f9f67f999456b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DRAWINGS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor receives and uses DRAWINGS provided by or requested from the Maintenance Surveyor for executing works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7b57445949baa2153e0f9f67f999456b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY WORK&quot;" target="&quot;WORK CLASSIFIED AS SUCH BY THE MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Emergency Work is defined and categorized by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY WORK&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR’S RESPONSIBILITY FOR STABILITY AND SAFETY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor must provide workmen and plant for emergency work without extra charge to the Employer except as detailed in the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY WORK&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Works Order is a standard directive for regular maintenance activities, while Emergency Work requires immediate attention without prior formal order but under Maintenance Surveyor's direction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a1ba1c6b232e9a68005845d332fa7552</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY WORK&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">25.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"EMERGENCY WORK may be carried out by others at the Employer's expense when the Contractor is unable or unwilling to do such work immediately, potentially leading to liquidated damages for non-compliance."&lt;SEP&gt;"In cases of emergency, the Contractor must immediately commence work without a formal Works Order but under strict supervision by the Maintenance Surveyor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contractor is required to commence Emergency Work immediately upon order from the Maintenance Surveyor unless otherwise instructed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1ba1c6b232e9a68005845d332fa7552</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMERGENCY WORK&quot;" target="&quot;WORKMEN&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Workmen may be employed to carry out EMERGENCY WORK when necessary and authorized by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR if the CONTRACTOR is unable or unwilling to do so immediately, potentially leading to liquidated damages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GENERAL HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;SUNDAY AND OTHER DAYS DECLARED AS GENERAL HOLIDAYS UNDER THE HOLIDAYS ORDINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A General Holiday includes Sundays and any other day officially declared a holiday by law."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GENERAL HOLIDAY&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Works ORDERS can include work on GENERAL HOLIDAYS, subject to certain conditions and permissions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIOD NAMED IN THE APPENDIX TO THE FORM OF TENDER CALCULATED FROM DATE OF COMPLETION CERTIFIED BY MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Period is determined based on the completion certification issued by the Maintenance Surveyor according to the terms specified in the tender form."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIALIST WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"During the Maintenance Period, the Contractor remains responsible for any Specialist Works not completed by the end of the works period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE PERIOD allows for any outstanding work on a WORKS ORDER after it has been substantially completed and passed final tests, during which the CONTRACTOR must complete remaining tasks as per Clause 56."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;COMPLETION CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Completion Certificate marks the start of the Maintenance Period for a part of the Works that has been completed and certified by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;SUSPENSION OF WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Suspension of Works can occur during the Maintenance Period for necessary reasons related to proper execution or safety."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"During the MAINTENANCE PERIOD, the CONTRACTOR must ensure temporary reinstatements are made good until full occupation for permanent reinstatement occurs."&lt;SEP&gt;"During the Maintenance Period, the Contractor is responsible for any necessary repairs or rectifications to ensure the Works meet contract specifications."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SITE is where the work takes place, and issues related to it are addressed during the MAINTENANCE PERIOD."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"During the Maintenance Period, the Employer retains certain rights over payments to sub-contractors through the Contractor, indicating a time-bound relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIOD&quot;" target="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENT CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An Interim Payment Certificate is related to the Maintenance Period during which the Contractor must ensure all works are executed satisfactorily before a final certificate can be issued."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor has authority over who can act as a Nominated Sub-contractor for executing parts of the Works."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor has the authority to nominate a Sub-Contractor for work under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2f5b22ce699e51609625c61aad79755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer nominates Nominated Sub-contractors who are employed by the Contractor for executing parts of the Works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2f5b22ce699e51609625c61aad79755</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR is responsible for carrying out works as detailed in a WORKS ORDER issued by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is not entitled to an extension if a Nominated Sub-contractor fails to commence or carry out work on time, unless the Contractor has taken all practical steps to prevent it."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG DOLLARS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"All payments under the CONTRACT will be made in HONG KONG DOLLARS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LAWS OF HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACT is governed by and construed according to the LAWS OF HONG KONG as specified in Clause (5)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE'S DELEGATION&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR'S ASSIGNMENT OR SUB-LETTING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">27.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Delegations from the Maintenance Surveyor to their representative can affect the Contractor’s ability to assign or sub-let, particularly in terms of written instructions and approvals required."&lt;SEP&gt;"Delegations from the representative can affect the Contractor’s ability to assign or sub-let, particularly in terms of written instructions and approvals required. The Maintenance Surveyor must act with the consent of the Employer for certain actions to be valid."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE'S DELEGATION&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The delegation from the Maintenance Surveyor to their representative can affect the Contractor’s ability to assign or sub-let. The Employer must approve forms of assignment and sub-contracting, impacting these delegations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S REPRESENTATIVE'S DELEGATION&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Delegations from the representative can affect the Contractor’s ability to assign or sub-let, particularly in terms of written instructions and approvals required. The Maintenance Surveyor must act with the consent of the Employer for certain actions to be valid."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTOR'S ASSIGNMENT OR SUB-LETTING&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer must consent to any assignment by the Contractor. The Employer also has a role in approving forms of sub-contracting and plant provision by subcontractors, impacting the validity of such actions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-contractors work under the Contractor, who must provide access to their sites for Maintenance Surveyor's inspection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The SUB-CONTRACTOR's sub-letting is subject to approval by the CONTRACTOR, who has responsibilities regarding their acts and defaults."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR can instruct removal of SUB-CONTRACTOR if necessary, ensuring no unreasonable exercise of power."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIAL CONDITION OF CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Special Conditions of Contract can override General Conditions if specified in the Special Condition itself."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIAL CONDITION OF CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer has conditions that require certain actions or insurances by the Contractor. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFICATION&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONSTRUCTOR must adhere to the SPECIFICATION, which is part of the CONTRACT DOCUMENTS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Specification offers detailed descriptions for the works that guide the Contractor's activities and are used by the Maintenance Surveyor for valuation purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b57445949baa2153e0f9f67f999456b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFICATION&quot;" target="&quot;SCHEDULE OF RATES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SCHEDULE OF RATES and SPECIFICATION are both used to detail works under a WORKS ORDER, guiding measurements and valuations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-62865738eafa658463c1c26212a98b20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SCHEDULE OF RATES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Schedule of Rates provides pricing information relevant to work execution, which is referenced in payment calculations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7b57445949baa2153e0f9f67f999456b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SCHEDULE OF RATES&quot;" target="&quot;TENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SCHEDULE OF RATES is referenced in the TENDER for payment of work executed under the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SCHEDULE OF RATES&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A WORKS ORDER shall be measured by the Contractor in accordance with the SCHEDULE OF RATES during its progress or after completion."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-62865738eafa658463c1c26212a98b20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 64&quot;" target="&quot;TESTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause 64 provides a mechanism to value and certify expenses related to certain tests not covered by the main contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 64&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause 64 is used to value and certify expenses related to uncovering or reinstating parts of the Works as directed by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 64&quot;" target="&quot;VARIATION ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLAUSE 64 is integral to the process of VARIATION ORDERS, which are deemed an indivisible part of Works Orders they vary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-62865738eafa658463c1c26212a98b20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUPERINTENDENCE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for providing SUPERINTENDENCE as per Clause 18, even when sub-contracting work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AMBIGUITIES OR DISCREPANCIES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR must follow instructions from the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR regarding AMBIGUITIES OR DISCREPANCIES within 14 days, ensuring clarity in contract interpretation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AMBIGUITIES OR DISCREPANCIES&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Ambiguities or discrepancies are terms the Maintenance Surveyor must clarify to ensure proper interpretation of contract documents, impacting project execution and compliance."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROVISION OF CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has authority over the PROVISION OF CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, including sub-contractors' activities on SITE AND/OR WORKS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKMEN OR AGENTS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has authority over WORKMEN or AGENTS of SUB-CONTRACTORS and can instruct their removal if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0764b1a02432b62a0ad22895f699b3d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR INSTRUCTIONS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Instructions from the Maintenance Surveyor guide contractors on how to perform their duties correctly during work execution."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR POWER TO INSTRUCT REMOVAL&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S POWER TO INSTRUCT REMOVAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor has the authority to instruct the removal of any sub-contractor from the site if deemed necessary for project management, indicating a significant supervisory role in construction projects like Kowloon Bay Data Centre Project."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S INSTRUCTIONS FOR AMBIGUITIES OR DISCREPANCIES (SUB-CLAUSE 5)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Instructions clarify ambiguous terms and resolve discrepancies, a key responsibility of the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TENDER&quot;" target="&quot;DIMENSION BOOK(S)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Dimension Book(s), submitted as part of the Tenders, is crucial for agreeing corrections with the Contractor during sample checking."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DRAWINGS PROVIDED BY THE CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DRAWINGS provided by the CONTRACTOR are used to define and measure WORKS as per the Schedule of Rates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DRAWINGS PROVIDED BY THE CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor approves technical drawings and documents submitted by the Contractor for work execution, ensuring they meet project requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;TEMPORARY WORKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Temporary Works are part of the overall Works, required for construction and maintenance as detailed by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2f5b22ce699e51609625c61aad79755</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">32.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONSTRUCTOR is responsible for executing and ensuring proper performance of the WORKS as per the CONTRACT terms. The design responsibility for PERMANENT WORK lies with the EMPLOYER under sub-clause 25."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for completing the WORKS as per the agreement with the EMPLOYER."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for executing the WORKS as per the contract terms, with a guarantee or deposit required to ensure due performance of the contract obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contractor executes the Works according to the contract terms, subject to suspension orders from the Maintenance Surveyor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contractor is responsible for executing and maintaining the Works, including any necessary repairs or rectifications within the Maintenance Period."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">45.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR designs TEMPORARY WORKS and has a role in supervising or controlling the Contractor's site operations, but is not directly responsible for PERMANENT WORK design as per sub-clause 25 of the CONTRACT."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has oversight over the execution of the WORKS and ensures they are carried out in strict accordance with the contract, unless legally or physically impossible."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor is responsible for surveying and certifying parts of the Works as completed to the Employer's satisfaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor oversees proposals related to pedestrian routes, lighting, guarding, and signing for road openings or traffic diversions on the Works."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor oversees the quality of works as per contractual requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor reviews and decides on matters related to the Works, ensuring their completion as per contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer receives the Works at the end of the Maintenance Period in a condition as specified by the Contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer takes over responsibility after 28 days from completion certification or earlier if they take over before that date."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;TESTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Tests are conducted to ensure quality of materials and workmanship in relation to the works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Site is a location where works are being carried out and maintained by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;SUSPENSION ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Suspension Orders from the Maintenance Surveyor can temporarily halt progress on the Works, affecting their completion timeline."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;DRAWINGS, SPECIFICATIONS, DETAILS OR LEVELS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Works progress is dependent on receiving necessary instructions and drawings from the Maintenance Surveyor for which specific applications were made in writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG GOVERNMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER may use information provided by the CONTRACTOR for specific purposes and the HONG KONG GOVERNMENT is involved in security arrangements as a guarantor or deposit holder."&lt;SEP&gt;"The HONG KONG GOVERNMENT, through its DIRECTOR OF ACCOUNTING SERVICES, is involved in managing security deposits from contractors on behalf of the EMPLOYER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG GOVERNMENT&quot;" target="&quot;DIRECTOR OF ACCOUNTING SERVICES, HONG KONG GOVERNMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The DIRECTOR OF ACCOUNTING SERVICES is an official of the HONG KONG GOVERNMENT responsible for receiving and managing security deposits from CONTRACTORS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S INSTRUCTIONS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is required to comply with MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR's instructions on matters related to the Contract, whether mentioned or not in the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S INSTRUCTIONS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR INSTRUCTIONS FOR AMBIGUITIES OR DISCREPANCIES (SUB-CLAUSE 5)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Instructions from the Maintenance Surveyor clarify ambiguous terms and resolve discrepancies between contract documents, ensuring clear interpretation by all parties involved in the Kowloon Bay Data Centre Project."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONSTRUCTOR is responsible for executing TEMPORARY WORKS designed by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR, but not liable for their design as per sub-clause 25 of the CONTRACT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR designs TEMPORARY WORKS, and their acts or neglect can contribute to damages, loss, or injury during execution of the CONTRACT as per sub-clause 25."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS AND RATES AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR's rates stated in his TENDER cover all risks, liabilities, and obligations set out or implied in the CONTRACT for executing the WORKS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUTHORIZED ENGLISH-SPEAKING AGENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is required to appoint an AUTHORIZED ENGLISH-SPEAKING AGENT who will be responsible for superintendence and communication with the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;AUTHORIZED ENGLISH-SPEAKING AGENT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has approval authority over the AUTHORIZED ENGLISH-SPEAKING AGENT appointed by the CONTRACTOR and can withdraw this approval if necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTORS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for employing SUB-CONTRACTORS to assist in executing the Works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CONTRACTORS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In case of contract termination due to special risks, sub-contractors are also required to remove their plant and equipment as per Employer's instructions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d995518579c80996691b5d1b66c19ea3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TECHNICAL PERSONNEL&quot;" target="&quot;SKILLED LABOUR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"TECHNICAL PERSONNEL are skilled and experienced, while SKILLED LABOUR is necessary for proper execution of works; both contribute to project success."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SEMI-SKILLED LABOUR&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR employs SEMI-SKILLED LABOUR as part of the workforce needed for timely and proper execution of Works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UNSKILLED LABOUR&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR also utilizes UNSKILLED LABOUR, which is necessary for the proper and timely execution of works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-49aef112fabf90ecd0181146a7452f1a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIALIST CONTRACTORS&quot;" target="&quot;UTILITY UNDERTAKERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both entities are involved in works on a site and must ensure safety measures are taken."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UTILITY UNDERTAKERS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR’S RESPONSIBILITY FOR STABILITY AND SAFETY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Specialist Contractors and utility undertakers are excluded from the Contractor's responsibility for stability and safety on the Site."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">62.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR delivers MATERIALS to the SITE for incorporation in the WORKS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for maintaining and cleaning the SITE after completing work."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contractor is responsible for maintaining the Site's orderliness and ensuring safety during construction activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contractor is responsible for work on the site and must comply with surveyor's orders regarding tests and inspections."&lt;SEP&gt;"The SITE is where the CONSTRUCTOR must carry out the WORKS, and if they fail to do so properly, the EMPLOYER can enter and expel them from it."&lt;SEP&gt;"The SITE where the works are carried out is relevant to the CONTRACTOR's operations and responsibilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Site is where Constructional Plant and Temporary Buildings are placed, managed, and eventually removed by the Contractor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Site is where the Contractor has access and limited occupation for executing the Works, as determined by the Employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2f5b22ce699e51609625c61aad79755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE&quot;" target="&quot;THE CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is responsible for maintaining records of labor, materials used on the Site daily as per Maintenance Surveyor's requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3e48c641bb7544fa8f59eeacc0c3c2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE&quot;" target="&quot;FOSSILS, COINS, ARTICLES OF VALUE OR ANTIQUITY, STRUCTURES, AND GEOLOGICAL OR ARCHAEOLOGICAL REMAINS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">4.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Site may contain valuable or historical items that are of interest to both the Employer and Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3e48c641bb7544fa8f59eeacc0c3c2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">10.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR certifies that the SITE has been cleared of surplus materials and left in a clean condition upon completion."&lt;SEP&gt;"The SITE is subject to inspections by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR for defects or imperfections that need investigation and rectification."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE&quot;" target="&quot;SITE CLEANLINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maintaining SITE cleanliness is a requirement as per the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR's instructions to ensure proper working conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE&quot;" target="&quot;ACCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Access to the site is granted to the Maintenance Surveyor for inspections and tests related to works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Works Orders dictate access and occupation of specific parts of the Site for the execution of works by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maintenance Surveyor's orders can affect the occupation and use of the Site by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER has ownership over materials at the SITE after COMPLETION and can take actions regarding surplus MATERIALS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Works Orders are executed on the Site, involving materials and goods that must be properly stored or protected."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WATCHMEN&quot;" target="&quot;PROVISION OF EMERGENCY STAFF WITHOUT EXTRA CHARGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Watchmen are part of emergency staff that the Contractor must provide without extra charge to the Employer except as detailed in the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR’S INSTRUCTIONS&quot;" target="&quot;CHECKING SETTING-OUT OR LINES/LEVELS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor can instruct on checking setting-out or lines/levels, which does not relieve the Contractor of his responsibility for correctness."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ORDERLY STATE OF SITE&quot;" target="&quot;SITE MANAGEMENT PRACTICES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Site management practices contribute to maintaining an orderly state of the site, which is important for avoiding danger to all persons."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CORRECTNESS OF POSITION, LEVEL, DIMENSIONS AND ALIGNMENT&quot;" target="&quot;SETTING-OUT OR LINES/LEVELS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Setting-out involves ensuring correctness of position, level, dimensions and alignment of all parts of the Works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CHECKING SETTING-OUT OR LINES/LEVELS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR’S DUTY TO RECTIFY ERRORS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is responsible for rectifying errors in setting-out or lines/levels at his own expense unless based on incorrect data provided by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE SAFETY MEASURES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR’S ONGOING RESPONSIBILITY FOR SITE STABILITY AND SAFETY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is responsible for keeping the Site and Works in an orderly state to avoid danger, providing lights, guards, fences, warning signs, and watchmen when necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0c2ce37d3bd5b0e583c4fe6bb69ef68b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIALIST WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIFICATION CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Specification Contractor is employed to execute Specialist Works separately identified in the Contract or any Works Order."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2f5b22ce699e51609625c61aad79755</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIALIST WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor issues certificates of completion for Specialist Works and determines when the Contractor's care responsibilities cease."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7e4b58ef0946f56f64c8c36cf13b78f9</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (4) OF THIS CLAUSE&quot;" target="&quot;EXCEPTED RISKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-clause 4 defines specific 'excepted risks' that absolve the contractor of responsibility for certain damages, losses, or injuries."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-7a4656c68f6e92038fab565bd5849a14</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAMAGE DUE TO MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S DESIGN&quot;" target="&quot;INDEMNIFICATION AGAINST LOSSES AND CLAIMS FOR INJURY OR DAMAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Damage due to the Maintenance Surveyor's design would be covered by indemnification against losses and claims for injury or damage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEGLECT OR DEFAULT BY EMPLOYER OR THEIR EMPLOYEES AND AGENTS IN COURSE OF EMPLOYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;INDEMNIFICATION AGAINST LOSSES AND CLAIMS FOR INJURY OR DAMAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Neglect by the Employer or their employees and agents would be covered under indemnification against losses and claims for injury or damage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INDEMNIFICATION AGAINST LOSSES AND CLAIMS FOR INJURY OR DAMAGE&quot;" target="&quot;RECOMPENSE FOR EMPLOYEE INJURY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Recompense for employee injury would be covered under indemnification against losses and claims for injury or damage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INDEMNIFICATION AGAINST LOSSES AND CLAIMS FOR INJURY OR DAMAGE&quot;" target="&quot;PROPORTIONATE LIABILITY REDUCTION DUE TO CONTRIBUTORY ACTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The proportionate liability reduction due to contributory acts would be considered in indemnification against losses and claims for injury or damage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5236112da700e89f157c80fd002a7fb7</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERMANENT WORK&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PERMANENT WORK is a part of the overall WORKS and its design responsibility lies with the EMPLOYER, while the CONSTRUCTOR ensures proper execution as per sub-clause 25 of the CONTRACT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERMANENT WORK&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The PERMANENT WORK design responsibility lies with the EMPLOYER and not the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR, according to sub-clause 25 of the CONTRACT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC ROADS OR FOOTPATHS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor must ensure that all operations do not interfere unnecessarily or improperly with public convenience and access to PUBLIC ROADS or FOOTPATHS during WORKS execution, as per sub-clause 26 of the CONTRACT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC ROADS OR FOOTPATHS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER provides access to PUBLIC ROADS or FOOTPATHS for the execution of WORKS and bears responsibility in cases where temporary works interfere with these public easements as per sub-clause 26 of the CONTRACT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC ROADS OR FOOTPATHS&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Public roads or footpaths may be affected by WORKS execution, potentially impacting access and use of PROPERTIES as per sub-clause 26 of the CONTRACT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTIES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is responsible for saving harmless and indemnifying the EMPLOYER in respect of all claims, demands, proceedings, damages, costs, charges and expenses related to PROPERTIES during WORKS execution as per sub-clause 26 of the CONTRACT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PROPERTIES&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER has rights over PROPERTIES, including access for executing WORKS, but is also responsible to indemnify the Contractor in certain circumstances related to these properties as per sub-clause 26 of the CONTRACT."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PUBLIC OR PRIVATE ROADS OR FOOTPATHS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is responsible for operations that should not interfere with public or private roads or footpaths during work execution."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER FOR LABOUR&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor must notify the Commissioner for Labour in case of workman injury, as per legal requirements. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER FOR LABOUR&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner for Labour requires notifications from the Contractor that shall be forwarded to the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATENT RIGHTS, DESIGN, TRADEMARK OR NAME&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer is protected from claims related to patent rights and other intellectual properties by the Contractor's indemnification obligation. "</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATENT RIGHTS&quot;" target="&quot;DESIGNS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Patent Rights and Designs are protected rights in respect of Constructional Plant, machine, work method or material required for the Works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATENT RIGHTS&quot;" target="&quot;TRADEMARK&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor shall indemnify from claims related to infringement of both patent rights and trademarks on materials used for the Works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PATENT RIGHTS&quot;" target="&quot;NAME RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Infringement of name or other protected rights, including patents, is covered under the same indemnification clause."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORK METHOD&quot;" target="&quot;MATERIAL&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Materials used in Work Methods, which may be patented or trademarked, fall under the same indemnification clause."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TONNAGE ROYALTIES&quot;" target="&quot;ROYALTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Tonnage royalties are a specific type of royalty mentioned within the context of material procurement for the Works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TONNAGE ROYALTIES&quot;" target="&quot;MATERIALS USED&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Tonnage Royalties refer to payments based on the weight of materials, which can be a financial aspect related to the procurement of resources for the project."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RENT&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both rent and payment fall under the category of fees required to be paid by the Contractor as per local or other duly constituted authority enactments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TENDER SUBMISSION DATE&quot;" target="&quot;NEW FEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The date of submission of the Tender is a condition precedent for any new fee imposed after that date, which would be at the expense of the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NEW FEE&quot;" target="&quot;INCREASE IN EXISTING FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An increase in existing fees, if applicable post-tender submission, will also be borne by the Contractor as a new fee."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1d7514d2843f8174e8fae404cc75760a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;SITE DIARY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor must deliver labor returns that are recorded in the Site Diary by an authorized agent or representative of the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;LABOR RETURNS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Labor Returns, which detail the numbers and classes of labor on-site, are provided by the Contractor to the Maintenance Surveyor's Representative daily."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;PENALTIES AND LIABILITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is responsible for indemnifying against penalties and liabilities arising from non-compliance with enactments, regulations, by-laws or rules."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;UTILITIES CONSUMPTION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Labor on-site consumes utilities, which must be recorded as part of the labor returns provided by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;THE EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer owns all discovered fossils and other valuable items; The Contractor must ensure these are not damaged or removed without permission from the Employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a3e48c641bb7544fa8f59eeacc0c3c2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE DIARY&quot;" target="&quot;LABOR ON-SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Labor on-site is recorded and documented in the Site Diary by the Maintenance Surveyor's Representative."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-949aa5f14dfe77c1d4658936c3d545de</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORK CARRIED OUT&quot;" target="&quot;LABOR ON-SITE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Labor on-site refers to workers engaged in various tasks related to maintenance or construction projects as documented in Site Diaries and Labor Returns, which are part of the Work Carried Out activities."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;OFFERING GRATUITIES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR must not offer gratuities or advantages to employees of the EMPLOYER, Maintenance Surveyor, or their staff without risking contract termination and liability for damages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contractors are required to engage labor both skilled and unskilled within Hong Kong."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"All notices related to the EMPLOYER must be served at their registered office in Hong Kong, as per Clause 93(2)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text mentions specific scenarios related to Hong Kong, indicating that it is a location of significance within this context."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d995518579c80996691b5d1b66c19ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;COMMISSIONER FOR LABOUR, HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Commissioner for Labour oversees and enforces compliance with labor conditions by contractors."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPEOPLE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maintenance Surveyors issue passes for workpeople and ensure their compliance with site regulations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKPEOPLE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contractors employ workpeople to carry out the works as per the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (B)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-clause B outlines the Contractor’s obligation to assist in conducting necessary tests and provide samples as required by surveyors."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (C)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-clause C defines responsibilities of the Maintenance Surveyor regarding testing, including costs and further actions if requirements are not met."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE [GCCBWT] 45&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-clause GCCBWT 45 ensures that the Contractor allows access by surveyors to all relevant areas of work, including workshops and storage places for materials supplied."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 46 (1)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause 46(1) outlines the requirement for the Contractor to allow the Maintenance Surveyor or his representative access and opportunity to examine work before covering it up."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 47 (2)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause 47(2) mandates that the Contractor must notify the Maintenance Surveyor for examination of work, ensuring his representative's timely presence when necessary."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS COMPLETION TIME&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is responsible for completing Works within specified times, as stated in Works Orders or a reasonable time if not stated."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS COMPLETION TIME&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer sets expectations for Works completion times through issued Works Orders, impacting the Contractor’s schedule."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NORMAL WORKING HOURS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is restricted from working outside NORMAL WORKING HOURS without permission, except in emergencies."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTINUOUS WORKING&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR can order CONTINUOUS WORKING at any time of the day or night."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXTENSION OF TIME FOR COMPLETION&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR may be granted EXTENSIONS OF TIME for COMPLETION if delays are reported to the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR within 42 days."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXTENSION OF TIME FOR COMPLETION&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has the authority to grant or deny EXTENSIONS OF TIME for COMPLETION based on reported delays."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INCLEMENT WEATHER CONDITIONS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Inclement weather conditions can be cited by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR as a cause for delay in work progress."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STORM SIGNAL NO. 8 OR ABOVE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The presence of storm signal no. 8 or above can be cited by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR as a cause for delay in work progress."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 5, CLAUSE 63, CLAUSE 57 (2) (A) TO (D), CLAUSE 63&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clauses can be cited by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR as a cause for delay in work progress."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UTILITY UNDERTAKING, DULY CONSTITUTED AUTHORITY&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Utility undertakings or other authorities can be cited by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR as a cause for delay in work progress if they fail to commence or carry out their duties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE, PORTION OF SITE&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SITE and its portions are where the CONTRACTOR must complete the WORKS ORDER tasks, and delays can be caused by lack of occupation as per MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR instructions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 57 (2)(A) TO (D)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor uses Clause 57 (2)(A) to (D) as a basis for determining whether the Contractor is entitled to an extension of time due to certain circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR (CLAUSE)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause within MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR requires CONTRACTOR to provide detailed information about delays and progress in writing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-671cf14fabde451a853f4cb49e6a812f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SITE OFFICES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for maintaining SITE OFFICES until all outstanding work is completed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a0c2d16f0534b8f7a9f0c286e3e24591</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUSPENSION ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;SUSPENSION LASTING MORE THAN 90 DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Suspension Order that lasts more than 90 days can have significant financial implications for the Contractor, potentially leading to additional expenditure claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 59(2)&quot;" target="&quot;GROUND REINSTATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause 59(2) excludes certain works related to ground reinstatement from being considered in Certificates of Completion."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY REINSTATEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER is responsible for any damage or injury arising from the CONTRACTOR's failure to comply with obligations related to temporary reinstatements during the MAINTENANCE PERIOD."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERMANENT REINSTATEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"At the end of the MAINTENANCE PERIOD, if permanent reinstatement is required by an authority or other party, the CONTRACTOR must ensure temporary reinstatements are made good until such time."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERMANENT REINSTATEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR advises on when permanent reinstatement should be carried out by the appropriate authority or another party, rather than the CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEFECT, IMPERFECTION OR FAULT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for investigating and rectifying any DEFECTS, IMPERFECTIONS, or FAULTS in the work they perform under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VARIATION ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR must comply with any Variation Order issued by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR and is responsible for executing such changes at their own expense."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-62865738eafa658463c1c26212a98b20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFICATION OR SCHEDULE OF RATES&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Specification or Schedule of Rates provides the baseline for rates that can be varied through orders from the Maintenance Surveyor, and any variations must be agreed upon based on these documents."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d72604c877ec1b265cace0cc38e4690d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIFICATION OR SCHEDULE OF RATES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor uses the Specification or Schedule of Rates as a reference for work and materials, especially when variations are made from these documents to determine new rates through agreement with the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d72604c877ec1b265cace0cc38e4690d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;VARIATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is responsible for executing work as per variation orders issued by the Maintenance Surveyor, which may include additions, omissions, substitutions, or alterations in quality and form of work specified in the Schedule of Rates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d72604c877ec1b265cace0cc38e4690d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DAYWORK BASIS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor can order works to be carried out on a daywork basis, determining payment rates which must be agreed upon with the Contractor or set by the surveyor if not already included in the contract terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d72604c877ec1b265cace0cc38e4690d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DRAWINGS, SPECIFICATION, DETAILS OR LEVELS FROM THE MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor needs instructions from the Maintenance Surveyor regarding necessary drawings and specifications to proceed with work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DRAWINGS, SPECIFICATION, DETAILS OR LEVELS FROM THE MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"These documents guide contractors on how to perform their tasks accurately as per project requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S OPINION ON REIMBURSEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor has discretion in determining if and how expenditures should be reimbursed, impacting financial claims under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISTURBANCE OF THE PROGRESS OF THE WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;WRITTEN APPLICATION BY THE CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor can apply to the Maintenance Surveyor for reimbursement if progress is disturbed due to specific reasons outlined in the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTOR’S PROPOSED DAYWORK ACTIVITIES&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor verifies proposed daywork activities to ensure they align with project requirements and contractual obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;REIMBURSEMENT OF EXPENDITURES&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor can apply for reimbursement based on daywork activities and other specific conditions outlined in the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c0c5e3d59d6713fc43836ebeb09b59a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT 51&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Works Order modifications are based on Contract 51 provisions for work execution timeline adjustments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT 51&quot;" target="&quot;UTILITY UNDERTAKING&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Utility undertakings not engaged by Employer can cause delays affecting Works completion timeline as per Contract 51."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACT 51&quot;" target="&quot;INGRESS/EGRESS CHANGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Changes to ingress or egress can affect work execution timeline as per Contract 51 provisions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM NOTICE PERIOD (28 DAYS)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor must be notified within the claim notice period if a Contractor intends to claim additional payment or higher rates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM NOTICE PERIOD (28 DAYS)&quot;" target="&quot;SUB-CLAUSE (2) CLAUSE 64, SUB-CLAUSE (2) CLAUSE 65&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-clauses of Clauses 64 and 65 specify the notice period for claims regarding higher rates or additional payments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM NOTICE PERIOD (28 DAYS)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL CLAIMS PROCEDURE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contractual claims procedure includes notice periods for claiming additional payments or higher rates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM NOTICE PERIOD (28 DAYS)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL CLAIM HANDLING PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contractual claim handling procedures include notice periods for claims regarding additional payments and higher rates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DRAWINGS, SPECIFICATIONS, DETAILS OR LEVELS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"These documents provide guidance on how the Contractor should perform their tasks accurately."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INGRESS/EGRESS CHANGES&quot;" target="&quot;WORK INGRESS/EGRESS MODIFICATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Work ingress or egress modifications can affect changes to ingress or egress as per contract conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;GENERAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT, SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIM PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"General and Special Conditions of Contract govern the claim process including notice periods and documentation requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTEMPORARY RECORDS&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIM DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contemporary records are necessary to support any claim, as per documentation requirements outlined in the contract conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTEMPORARY RECORDS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contemporary records are kept by the Contractor to support claims, which must be reviewed and approved by the Maintenance Surveyor for accuracy."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM PROCESS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL OBLIGATIONS AND PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contractual obligations and provisions define the claim process, including notice periods and documentation requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM PROCESS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTUAL OBLIGATIONS AND RIGHTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Contractual obligations and rights govern the claim process, including notice periods and documentation requirements."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;UTILITY UNDERTAKING NOT ENGAGED BY EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;WORK METHODOLOGY CHANGES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Utility undertakings not engaged by Employer can cause changes in work methodology affecting project execution."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS COMPLETION TIMELINE&quot;" target="&quot;MATERIAL DELIVERY DELAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Material delivery delays can affect Works completion timeline as per contract conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS COMPLETION TIMELINE&quot;" target="&quot;WORK EXECUTION TIMELINE ADJUSTMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Work execution timeline adjustments can affect the overall Works completion timeline as per contract conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTUAL CLAIMS PROCEDURE&quot;" target="&quot;WORK EXECUTION IMPACT FACTORS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Impact factors on work execution can trigger the claim procedure as per contract conditions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORK ORDER MODIFICATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;WORK EXECUTION IMPACT FACTORS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Work order modifications can impact work execution factors such as sequence, method, and timing of construction."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTUAL COMPLIANCE&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIM DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Compliance with contractual conditions requires proper documentation for claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;CLAIM NOTIFICATION PERIODS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Notification periods for claims require proper documentation to support any claims made by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF CONTRACT also define claim provisions that apply to specific situations or clauses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAIM&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has a role in processing and considering CLAIMS from the CONTRACTOR."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has the authority to consider and process CLAIMS from the CONTRACTOR within specified timeframes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR may instruct on NOTICE requirements and record-keeping for CLAIMS."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;RECORDS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for maintaining RECORDS to support any claims made under the contract clauses."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FIRST INTERIM ACCOUNT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR receives a FIRST INTERIM ACCOUNT from the CONTRACTOR detailing the sum claimed and grounds for it."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FURTHER UP-TO-DATE ACCOUNTS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR provides FURTHER UP-TO-DATE ACCOUNTS to update claims as necessary, per MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR's instructions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FURTHER UP-TO-DATE ACCOUNTS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Further up-to-date accounts detailing accumulated totals of claims need approval from the Maintenance Surveyor to ensure they are accurate."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR(S)&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">17.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer can make direct payments to Nominated Sub-contractors if certain conditions are met, establishing a financial and legal connection between them."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer has the right to order work or materials from Nominated Sub-contractors and can instruct the Contractor to enter into subcontracts with them using specific forms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTOR(S)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">14.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor has obligations towards Nominated Sub-contractors that can be assigned by the Employer after the Maintenance Period, suggesting a contractual and operational connection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contractor is required to enter into a sub-contract with the Nominated Sub-contractor as instructed by the Maintenance Surveyor, and must use the standard form of sub-contract provided by the Employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR (CLAUSE 69)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor has significant supervisory roles in the project, including instructing contractors on sub-contracts with different terms from standard forms and making decisions that impact payment and project continuation."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STANDARD FORM OF SUB-CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor can instruct the Contractor to enter into a sub-contract with different terms from those specified in the Standard Form, affecting how obligations are discharged under the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S INSTRUCTION&quot;" target="&quot;SUB-CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maintenance Surveyor's Instruction can lead to entering into a sub-contract with a Nominated Sub-contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S INSTRUCTION UNDER CLAUSE 68(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maintenance Surveyor's Instruction under Clause 68(2) can result in a sub-contract being entered into with a Nominated Sub-contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S INSTRUCTION UNDER CLAUSE 69(2)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Maintenance Surveyor's Instruction under Clause 69(2) can lead to the Contractor entering into a sub-contract with a Nominated Sub-contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUB-CONTRACT&quot;" target="&quot;HIRE OR HIRE-PURCHASE AGREEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Sub-contractors may be involved in hire or hire-purchase agreements for constructional plant usage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTOR'S OBJECTION&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor may raise objections against the nomination of a Nominated Sub-contractor, which must be addressed by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;QUOTATIONS, INVOICES, VOUCHERS AND RECEIPTS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is required to provide these documents related to expenditure in respect of Nominated Sub-contractors as instructed by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;QUOTATIONS, INVOICES, VOUCHERS AND RECEIPTS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"These documents provide financial details related to expenditures in respect of Nominated Sub-contractors and require the Maintenance Surveyor's approval for payment."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTORS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is responsible for paying Nominated Sub-contractors as directed by Maintenance Surveyor certificates."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOMINATED SUB-CONTRACTORS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR CERTIFICATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Certificates issued by the Maintenance Surveyor determine payments due to Nominated Sub-contractors."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The certificate issued by the Maintenance Surveyor certifies payments due, impacting financial claims under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT AND TEMPORARY BUILDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor owns constructional plant and temporary buildings that vest in the Employer upon site arrival, showing an ownership transfer during project execution."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT AND TEMPORARY BUILDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Constructional Plant and Temporary Buildings owned by the Contractor become property of the Employer when brought onto the Site, establishing a property rights relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERIALS FOR INCORPORATION IN WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor owns materials for incorporation in works that vest in the Employer upon delivery to the site, indicating an ownership transfer during project execution."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERIALS FOR INCORPORATION IN WORKS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Materials owned by the Contractor become property of the Employer when delivered to the Site and can only be removed with consent or upon surplus determination, showing a property rights relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;TEMPORARY BUILDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for removing TEMPORARY BUILDINGS from the SITE after COMPLETION unless otherwise specified by CLAUSE 74."&lt;SEP&gt;"The TEMPORARY BUILDINGS are part of the WORKS and their use is subject to agreement with the EMPLOYER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SURPLUS MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The SURPLUS MATERIALS revert to the ownership of the EMPLOYER, and the CONTRACTOR is responsible for their removal or disposal as per CLAUSE 74."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HIRE OR HIRE-PURCHASE AGREEMENT&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Works Order can be linked to hire or hire-purchase agreement for constructional plant use in completing works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOSS OF OR DAMAGE TO CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT&quot;" target="&quot;SUBMISSIONS* FOR PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Submissions for payment may include claims related to loss or damage of constructional plant, impacting the cost recovery process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SUBMISSIONS* FOR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Submissions for payment are subject to checking and correction by the Maintenance Surveyor before being processed."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIMENSION BOOK(S)&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"DIMENSION BOOK(S) are required for each WORKS ORDER, providing necessary details for measurement and valuation of work executed under that order."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIMENSION BOOK(S)&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR is responsible for supplying DIMENSION BOOK(S), which are set out by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR and must include supporting documents as required."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIMENSION BOOK(S)&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR determines the manner in which DIMENSION BOOK(S) are set out and may require supporting documents for payment claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DIMENSION BOOK(S)&quot;" target="&quot;APPENDIX TO THE FORM OF TENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Dimension Books must be submitted as per the schedule set out in the Appendix to the Form of Tender upon substantial completion."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CERTIFICATES FOR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Certificates for payment are based on the completion of WORKS ORDERS, ensuring accurate billing and payments to the CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CERTIFICATES FOR PAYMENT&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Certificates issued by the Maintenance Surveyor certify the correct value of completed works, impacting payments under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPENDIX TO THE FORM OF TENDER&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Works Orders, sorted by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR according to their claimed value as stated in the APPENDIX TO THE FORM OF TENDER, will be batched for payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-77cf568578b8488d566bb45f92f61c0d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS ORDERS&quot;" target="&quot;COMPLAINT CHITS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both Works Orders and Complaint Chits are subject to batched sampling checks by the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS ORDERS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR is involved in certifying costs for WORKS ORDERS issued to the CONTRACTOR, impacting financial settlements between parties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS ORDERS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The WORKS ORDERS issued prior to re-entry may affect the payment due to the CONTRACTOR if completion is delayed, potentially leading to additional payments for excess work or liquidated damages."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;APPENDIX TO FORM OF TENDER&quot;" target="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Appendix to Form of Tender specifies conditions under which Interim Payments can be made and their maximum percentage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor has the authority to certify and make interim payments based on work completed."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Interim Payments are made in relation to Works Orders exceeding a certain value as specified by the Form of Tender Appendix."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FORM OF TENDER&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Works Orders are referenced within the Form of Tender, particularly regarding payment thresholds and values."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 79A&quot;" target="&quot;CLAUSE 80A&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause 79A determines applicability of Clause 80A for claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 79B&quot;" target="&quot;CLAUSE 80B&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clause 79B determines applicability of Clause 80B for claims."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;HONG KONG SUPREME COURT&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT ON CERTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Hong Kong Supreme Court's Rules determine interest rates and payment procedures in case of overpayment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE LAWS OF HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Laws of Hong Kong define the rights and obligations of the Employer, including their power to deduct payments from the Contractor for overpayment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;THE LAWS OF HONG KONG&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Laws of Hong Kong outline the responsibilities and protections afforded to the Contractor in terms of payment and work approval."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENT CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer can issue an Interim Payment Certificate which may be corrected or modified by the Maintenance Surveyor and is not deemed to constitute approval of work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INTERIM PAYMENT CERTIFICATE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"An Interim Payment Certificate is issued in relation to a Works Order under the Contract but does not constitute approval of work or protect the Contractor from over-measurement or overpayment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 49&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLAUSE 49 defines conditions under which the EMPLOYER can take action against the CONTRACTOR regarding commencement of works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 48&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLAUSE 48 outlines actions by the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR that can lead to consequences for the CONTRACTOR if not followed properly."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 48&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR certifies work completion for payment under CLAUSE 48 regarding permanent work condemnation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d02dce26d755dbc2a1f010f8cd0550db</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 48&quot;" target="&quot;SPECIAL RISKS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Special risks affect the interpretation and application of CLAUSE 48, particularly concerning permanent work condemnation."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d02dce26d755dbc2a1f010f8cd0550db</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 72 AND 73&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Under CLAUSE 72 AND 73, unused or partially used MATERIALS become property of the EMPLOYER if the CONTRACTOR is expelled from the SITE."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 62&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The provisions of CLAUSE 62 apply for attendance by the CONTRACTOR for measurement and agreement of records, which are relevant to their obligations under the contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 62&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLAUSE 62 provides rights and procedures for the EMPLOYER in relation to measurements and agreements with the CONTRACTOR regarding work completion."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MATERIALS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONTRACTOR may have agreements or contracts related to MATERIALS that are subject to assignment as per CLAUSE 59."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKMEN&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The WORKMEN, employed by the EMPLOYER, will complete works after the removal of the CONTRACTOR and their costs must be accounted for before payment can be made to the CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKMEN&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR can authorize WORKMEN from other contractors to carry out necessary works if the CONTRACTOR fails to comply with instructions within a reasonable time."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 59&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLAUSE 59 defines conditions for assigning agreements or contracts, impacting the financial obligations of the CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 59&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"CLAUSE 59 outlines conditions under which the EMPLOYER may require assignment of agreements, impacting financial obligations and payment terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 59&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR plays a role in certifying costs and expenses related to work carried out under CLAUSE 59, impacting financial settlements between the CONTRACTOR and EMPLOYER."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIODS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE PERIODS are relevant to determining when payments can be made to the CONTRACTOR after their removal from a project site."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE PERIODS&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE PERIODS are critical for determining when payments can be made to the CONTRACTOR after their removal from a project site, as defined by the EMPLOYER's obligations."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIAL RISKS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor is required to use best endeavours to complete execution of works during certain specified 'special risks' events. The Employer can terminate the contract in such cases but must pay for completed work and preliminary items."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d995518579c80996691b5d1b66c19ea3</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIAL RISKS&quot;" target="&quot;CLAUSE 72&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The occurrence of special risks impacts how property is deemed to be of the EMPLOYER under CLAUSE 72 for claims and indemnification purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d02dce26d755dbc2a1f010f8cd0550db</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;SPECIAL RISKS&quot;" target="&quot;WAR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Special Risks include events such as war that can cause destruction or damage, leading to disputes between EMPLOYER and CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5fa9c6366e076e445101d83858797035</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 72&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">5.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR also plays a role in determining the property deemed to be of the EMPLOYER under CLAUSE 72 for claims and indemnification purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d02dce26d755dbc2a1f010f8cd0550db</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WAR&quot;" target="&quot;DISPUTE SETTLEMENT MECHANISM&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Dispute Settlement Mechanisms are invoked in cases of WAR and other special risks, providing a framework for resolving conflicts between EMPLOYER and CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5fa9c6366e076e445101d83858797035</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE SETTLEMENT MECHANISM&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT TERMINATION/BREACH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"In the event of contract termination or breach due to special risks like WAR, DISPUTE SETTLEMENT MECHANISMS are used for resolution between EMPLOYER and CONTRACTOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5fa9c6366e076e445101d83858797035</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DISPUTE SETTLEMENT MECHANISM&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor resolves conflicts between the Employer and Contractor through written decisions, ensuring project continuity."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S DECISION&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACT TERMINATION/BREACH&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR's decisions can lead to contract termination or breach, affecting the DISPUTE SETTLEMENT MECHANISM."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-5fa9c6366e076e445101d83858797035</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR'S DECISION&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Decisions made by the Maintenance Surveyor are binding and impact payment and project continuation."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Any dispute involving the CONTRACTOR and MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR can be referred to an ARBITRATOR for resolution under the Lands and Works Model Arbitration Rules."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">15.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR's decisions in disputes with the CONTRACTOR can be challenged through arbitration, as per Clause 93(2)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor may be involved in disputes or differences, with an Arbitrator hearing evidence from witnesses including the Maintenance Surveyor."</data>
  <data key="d6">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;LANDS AND WORKS MODEL ARBITRATION RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Lands and Works Model Arbitration Rules govern how arbitrations are conducted in disputes involving the CONTRACTOR and MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATOR&quot;" target="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Disputes involving the EMPLOYER can be referred to an ARBITRATOR, as per Clause 94(1)."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARBITRATION ORDINANCE&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Works Order can be referred to arbitration if either party is dissatisfied with a Maintenance Surveyor's decision, subject to the provisions of the Arbitration Ordinance."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 79 AND CLAUSE 81&quot;" target="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD (14 DAYS)&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Clauses 79 and 81 specify conditions for payment that trigger a Notice Period of 14 days if not met by the Employer."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CLAUSE 79 AND CLAUSE 81&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Failure to pay as per Clauses 79 and 81 within the specified period allows for Contract Termination by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NOTICE PERIOD (14 DAYS)&quot;" target="&quot;TERMINATION OF CONTRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Notice Period of 14 days, if not honored by the Employer, leads to the possibility of Contract Termination by the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">86.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The EMPLOYER provides information to the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR through Contract documents which are not to be divulged outside of contract purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer engages utility undertakings and supplies materials that can affect the progress of works, impacting the Maintenance Surveyor's role."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer has a role in approving forms of assignment by the Contractor. The Maintenance Surveyor must act with the consent of the Employer for certain actions to be valid."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employer is involved in receiving interim payments certified by the Maintenance Surveyor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR acts on behalf of the EMPLOYER to enforce removal or sale of CONSTRUCTIONAL PLANT, TEMPORARY BUILDINGS, and SURPLUS MATERIALS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR advises on work that may be necessary, particularly in cases where permanent reinstatement is required by an authority or other party."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR certifies payments to the CONTRACTOR and passes certificates to the EMPLOYER for final payment approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has discretion to decide who conducts investigations of defects and can instruct the EMPLOYER's own or other contractors for this purpose if needed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor acts on behalf of both the Employer's interests in overseeing the Works and ensuring proper execution during the Maintenance Period."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor certifies payments due to Nominated Sub-contractors which the Employer must honor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor is distinct from the Employer and serves as a separate point of contact for notices under the Contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor is responsible for evaluating claims made by the Contractor, and these evaluations can affect the Employer's liability."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor's decisions are final and binding upon the Employer unless either party requires arbitration."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;PAYMENT ON CERTIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Employer makes payments based on certificates issued by the Maintenance Surveyor and may deduct overpayments from future payments or issue demand notes."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">225.0</data>
  <data key="d5">The CONTRACTOR and EMPLOYER have a comprehensive contractual relationship involving financial, operational, and legal agreements related to construction projects. Both parties are bound by specific obligations defined in their contract, with the EMPLOYER having significant authority over the CONTRACTOR's actions regarding works execution.

Both entities can refer disputes to arbitration if they are dissatisfied with decisions made by a Maintenance Surveyor or if no decision is given within 90 days. The CONTRACTOR and EMPLOYER have financial agreements where payments for completed work, preliminary items, and costs incurred are based on interim payment certificates submitted by the CONTRACTOR.

The EMPLOYER becomes the owner of materials delivered to the site upon completion and has rights over surplus materials after project completion. Conversely, the CONTRACTOR is obligated to complete Works Orders within a prescribed time frame; failure to do so may result in liquidated damages being imposed by the EMPLOYER.

Financial responsibilities are shared between both parties: The EMPLOYER can make payments on behalf of the CONTRACTOR if wages are not paid as required and has the authority to deduct certain amounts from payments due to the CONTRACTOR under various provisions. Additionally, the EMPLOYER indemnifies the CONTRACTOR against special risks while also being potentially liable for claims made by the CONTRACTOR.

The CONTRACTOR is responsible for completing works orders and may face liquidated damages if not completed within the prescribed time frame; they are obligated to submit statements to the EMPLOYER and receive payments based on interim payment certificates. The EMPLOYER has the authority to have work carried out by the CONTRACTOR or directly pay nominated sub-contractors, with rights over plant provision and approval of forms.

The relationship between both parties is governed by clauses that define information exchange, obligations, security deposits for due performance, and potential termination conditions based on special risks. The EMPLOYER can make deductions from payments to the CONTRACTOR if there are overpayments or other causes as defined under Hong Kong laws.</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-d02dce26d755dbc2a1f010f8cd0550db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f144b21e5d9d4c86fe6de033c3b52697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d995518579c80996691b5d1b66c19ea3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3df24d7cf0a0114d43ffbcf5d5c71fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba22dc0a0fc19429a484bb41c261d34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef86c4247fdecc339b1414a3fdd5966&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f19199388ebb0416790d9140af888a4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa9c6366e076e445101d83858797035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON NAMED AS SUCH IN ARTICLES OF AGREEMENT OR APPOINTED BY EMPLOYER AND NOTIFIED TO CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Maintenance Surveyor is either named in the contract or appointed by the Employer with written notification to the Contractor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">55.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR evaluates whether a WORKS ORDER has been substantially completed and issues a Certificate of Completion, determining any liquidated damages for delay if the work is not finished on time."&lt;SEP&gt;"The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has the authority to issue orders and permissions related to WORKS ORDERS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor considers extensions related to the completion of tasks specified in the Works Order."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor has authority to make corrections and modifications in any previous certificate issued by them, withholding certificates if not satisfied with work execution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor issues and certifies payment for works orders that comply with the contract terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Maintenance Surveyor issues written orders (Works Orders) to the Contractor detailing work or services to be executed under the Contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works Orders are issued by the Maintenance Surveyor to direct and sanction specific works, including Emergency Work."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2f5b22ce699e51609625c61aad79755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87f722c8522f822c2e90eb078db141b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1ba1c6b232e9a68005845d332fa7552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;" target="&quot;EMERGENCY WORKS ORDERED&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Maintenance Surveyor can order Emergency Works from time to time which fall under the broader scope of the Works."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-f2f5b22ce699e51609625c61aad79755</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">327.0</data>
  <data key="d5">The CONTRACTOR and MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR are key entities in a construction project, each with distinct roles and responsibilities. The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has significant authority over the CONTRACTOR's work, including issuing instructions, approving works, certifying costs, and overseeing compliance with contractual standards.

The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR is responsible for measuring and certifying payments to the CONTRACTOR based on completed work. They can withhold or grant permission regarding the use of constructional plant by the CONTRACTOR on site. The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR also has authority over interim payment certificates, corrections, modifications, and variations in works orders. They issue notices and authorize actions that the CONTRACTOR must follow diligently; any disputes with these decisions can only be contested through arbitration within 90 days.

The CONTRACTOR is responsible for executing work under a WORKS ORDER as per MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR's satisfaction and instructions, including responding to maintenance requirements during and after the Maintenance Period. The CONTRACTOR must submit bills, dimension books, claims for interim payments, notifications about delays or probable extent of causes, worker injuries, and intentions to claim additional payment within 28 days.

The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR has authority over the removal of constructional plant, temporary buildings, and surplus materials from the site after completion. They can instruct the CONTRACTOR on sub-contracts and related matters, including handling objections from the Contractor. The MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR also evaluates claims submitted by the CONTRACTOR within a specified timeframe.

Both parties share liability in cases where their respective acts or neglect contribute to damages, loss, or injury during work execution. The CONTRACTOR must notify the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR about delays and probable extent when causes are apparent, as well as intentions to claim additional payment within 28 days of an event becoming apparent.

In summary, the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR plays a crucial role in overseeing the work executed by the CONTRACTOR, ensuring compliance with contractual standards, approving works, certifying costs and expenses, issuing certificates for payments, and handling claims. The CONTRACTOR must adhere to these instructions and notifications while executing their responsibilities under the WORKS ORDER.</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-599efa27c5ee543ca385bb3d944e13fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb73081d4183e7d829a503c9bb63a946&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5861f6b1612f2edfb0a3b893d8508a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ce0f4a340a17df1f53274ac940867b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b57445949baa2153e0f9f67f999456b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d204e5d2ccca14fb7f49bf493cc0bdb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0c5dc907f05ceb93ea74513adac240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf1f3e50c00eb564c5a2c138e90383e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c0a211cf707d60ea80e6c68ae9e2599&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff7b29e752b0e4f9e3121c55ee790b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19910b7f9bd42f1fa47e38d5d59bbb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522c43aa0cb7d424d1da1c5b00c65777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ba22dc0a0fc19429a484bb41c261d34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b3528cf552045555b1e6ac732dd25a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32963fd7d32ec116c9715aae3cbcb4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d288eda39d01e6178bcf7c5f4500b57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-affc5866b16d32a569c7ab46b9093e2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c58277d66887ed610fbaec73a4e8d85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-983418f16d72d20a53c38b36bcb45ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fb1308c02d44b7ab0dcb7b386e3c410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c2d16f0534b8f7a9f0c286e3e24591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1373b3be58ae445e60a533999b71823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-534e9d84651f98c51ccc8c24e68050b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec39c2912df341528c1942c4d7a77e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8130c8086938f6df2d05cdf9fb7e405c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c78f2f44e3406d58803bc69cd6892eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5353a0b04268f3f2bf8419dceec4f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa9c6366e076e445101d83858797035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b303be3f296ee1a255a0d6e39708e058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d72604c877ec1b265cace0cc38e4690d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e827172d85d4fce202f234f783e044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1ba1c6b232e9a68005845d332fa7552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ff1f20b792fbc8d1bdd961c49e1244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6fcfdf9559a5ecd190189bd2dc1bf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671cf14fabde451a853f4cb49e6a812f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62865738eafa658463c1c26212a98b20</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORKS ORDER&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;">
  <data key="d4">74.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The CONSTRUCTOR is responsible for carrying out the WORKS ORDER as specified in the contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CONTRACTOR must complete WORKS ORDERS within specified times, with provisions for extensions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Contractor is responsible for completing tasks detailed in the Works Order and can seek extensions based on specific conditions outlined in Clause 57."&lt;SEP&gt;"The WORKS ORDER details tasks for which the CONTRACTOR must provide updates on potential delays to the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR."&lt;SEP&gt;"The WORKS ORDER is a document that specifies tasks for the CONTRACTOR under the Contract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The WORKS ORDER is related to the claims process, as it defines the scope of work for which claims can be made."&lt;SEP&gt;"The WORKS ORDER serves as a written order from the MAINTENANCE SURVEYOR, directing the CONSTRUCTOR on specific works to be executed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Works Order is a document that directs the Contractor what needs to be done, with specific timeframes and requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"WORKS ORDER directs the CONSTRUCTOR on specific parts of the Works, which must be executed according to Maintenance Surveyor’s directions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Works Orders document specific tasks or work items assigned to the Contractor, guiding their execution and payment."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e2d562d8afcd917deebad02c95fa56d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d9e511550fbff7a251d73498bcd64d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b57445949baa2153e0f9f67f999456b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06b2afedf5ae2df469662b1c2af2820d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c2d16f0534b8f7a9f0c286e3e24591&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ac9b93ec382ad9a1bb20e1b7960a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b46e3164fc93eef619ecf2b2643e1002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671cf14fabde451a853f4cb49e6a812f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61507c5493c688feb54013b712e53b53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f6be589350c8e73f0a57d60397f9eb</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON WHOSE TENDER HAS BEEN ACCEPTED BY THE EMPLOYER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Contractor is an individual or company that accepts a tender from the Employer to execute Works under the Contract."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-abfa4c447132cda1acca49de3797a9c4</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;CONTRACTOR&quot;" target="&quot;CLAUSE 48 OR CLAUSE 49&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The Contractor must comply with clauses related to work commencement and progress, which are critical for avoiding Forfeiture as per Clause 87."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9ba22dc0a0fc19429a484bb41c261d34</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
</graph></graphml>